1
00:01:33,604 --> 00:01:35,854
We're the only two survivors
from our company.

2
00:01:38,646 --> 00:01:39,687
We have won,

3
00:01:40,937 --> 00:01:42,437
but this is the price of war.

4
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:46,479
They paid a far greater price than we did.

5
00:01:47,521 --> 00:01:50,604
We killed more than
1,000 Pakistani soldiers.

6
00:01:52,312 --> 00:01:53,396
It's not about them.

7
00:01:55,062 --> 00:01:56,521
{\an8}It's about our soldiers.

8
00:01:57,604 --> 00:01:59,104
That's why I'm here.

9
00:02:02,229 --> 00:02:04,146
This was neither the first war
nor the last.

10
00:02:06,104 --> 00:02:09,229
But the wars to come
will not end like this.

11
00:02:19,812 --> 00:02:21,146
A secret program.

12
00:02:24,229 --> 00:02:27,354
To prepare the next generation
of Indian soldiers.

13
00:02:28,729 --> 00:02:32,562
{\an8}Soldiers who will rewrite the rules
of warfare.

14
00:02:35,479 --> 00:02:37,396
I have the trial permission.

15
00:02:39,896 --> 00:02:42,604
But to make sure the program stays
permanent, I need you.

16
00:02:43,937 --> 00:02:44,979
{\an8}Why me?

17
00:02:46,687 --> 00:02:49,396
Because you know
the price of war, Guru <i>ji.</i>

18
00:03:18,812 --> 00:03:20,604
{\an8}India's most important offshore oilfield,

19
00:03:21,812 --> 00:03:22,812
Mumbai High,

20
00:03:24,187 --> 00:03:25,396
is in great danger.

21
00:03:32,187 --> 00:03:35,146
<i>Terrorists have attacked Mumbai High
via a sea route.</i>

22
00:03:35,729 --> 00:03:37,979
<i>Twenty-eight ONGC workers are being
held hostage.</i>

23
00:03:39,271 --> 00:03:41,812
<i>If we try to save them,</i>

24
00:03:42,187 --> 00:03:45,521
<i>they've threatened to blow up
the oil rig.</i>

25
00:03:46,396 --> 00:03:49,229
The terrorists have the hostages
and the first-mover advantage.

26
00:03:49,771 --> 00:03:50,979
How will you defeat them?

27
00:03:51,604 --> 00:03:52,562
Come in, Charlie One.

28
00:03:53,229 --> 00:03:55,104
This is Colonel Fateh Singh Lakhawat.

29
00:03:56,562 --> 00:03:58,228
<i>Team, proceed to target.</i>

30
00:03:58,229 --> 00:04:01,353
Risking such an important mission
with a new team?

31
00:04:01,354 --> 00:04:03,812
Not a risk. Guts.

32
00:04:05,646 --> 00:04:06,604
No guts…

33
00:04:07,979 --> 00:04:08,979
no glory.

34
00:04:11,104 --> 00:04:14,353
How can they breathe without
oxygen cylinders?

35
00:04:14,354 --> 00:04:17,854
{\an8}My soldiers can hold their breath
underwater for seven to nine minutes

36
00:04:18,312 --> 00:04:20,229
<i>without reducing their swimming speed.</i>

37
00:04:28,687 --> 00:04:30,770
<i>Alpha One. Fourteen targets in all, sir.</i>

38
00:04:30,771 --> 00:04:33,686
Seven on deck, four in the control room,

39
00:04:33,687 --> 00:04:35,771
and three on the lower level
with the hostages.

40
00:04:36,187 --> 00:04:39,937
They aren't wearing night vision glasses.
How can they still see?

41
00:04:40,271 --> 00:04:41,271
Dr. Cherian,

42
00:04:41,812 --> 00:04:43,728
they don't need to see

43
00:04:43,729 --> 00:04:45,104
because they can hear.

44
00:04:47,312 --> 00:04:50,437
<i>Their hearing ability beats
that of an ordinary person.</i>

45
00:04:52,229 --> 00:04:54,520
Come in, Charlie One. It's a go!

46
00:04:54,521 --> 00:04:55,396
Go.

47
00:04:55,854 --> 00:04:56,771
One shot.

48
00:04:58,646 --> 00:04:59,562
One kill.

49
00:05:02,562 --> 00:05:03,479
{\an8}No luck.

50
00:05:06,354 --> 00:05:07,271
{\an8}All skill.

51
00:05:17,729 --> 00:05:18,604
Bomb defused.

52
00:05:19,729 --> 00:05:20,978
Hostages released, sir.

53
00:05:20,979 --> 00:05:22,354
Move! To the exit!

54
00:05:22,562 --> 00:05:24,729
<i>Team terrorists, you lost!
Get up!</i>

55
00:05:26,604 --> 00:05:27,770
<i>Chin up, guys. Chin up!</i>

56
00:05:27,771 --> 00:05:29,396
<i>- Great job, guys.
- Well done, boys.</i>

57
00:05:33,396 --> 00:05:35,521
That was a war games exercise!

58
00:05:35,937 --> 00:05:39,186
Ladies and gentlemen,
presenting Team Alpha.

59
00:05:39,187 --> 00:05:41,354
The first. The fastest.

60
00:05:41,729 --> 00:05:42,687
The strongest.

61
00:05:43,729 --> 00:05:45,687
<i>Reflexes matching an eagle.</i>

62
00:05:47,562 --> 00:05:49,604
<i>Strength to floor wrestlers.</i>

63
00:05:51,104 --> 00:05:54,104
<i>They've run in
minus 30-degree temperatures,</i>

64
00:05:54,771 --> 00:05:56,270
<i>where most people struggle to breathe.</i>

65
00:05:56,271 --> 00:05:59,061
<i>India's most elite and advanced
commando program.</i>

66
00:05:59,062 --> 00:06:02,853
Human lethal weapons, with Alpha
running through their veins.

67
00:06:02,854 --> 00:06:05,437
{\an8}- Alpha?
- Yes, Alpha.

68
00:06:06,312 --> 00:06:08,646
{\an8}The team was injected with the serum,

69
00:06:09,354 --> 00:06:11,437
{\an8}then they were trained by our very best.

70
00:06:11,812 --> 00:06:13,979
Lt. Col. Vikrant Kaul.

71
00:06:15,396 --> 00:06:16,479
{\an8}My Guru <i>ji.</i>

72
00:06:19,062 --> 00:06:21,021
I lost an eye in the Kargil attack,

73
00:06:21,729 --> 00:06:24,646
{\an8}but my vision is sharper than ever.

74
00:06:24,979 --> 00:06:27,479
I trained Cobra, Ghatak
and many other teams,

75
00:06:27,729 --> 00:06:31,812
but I've never seen an attack team
like Alpha.

76
00:06:32,229 --> 00:06:33,396
{\an8}They're bloody good.

77
00:06:34,021 --> 00:06:35,312
And that's an understatement.

78
00:06:36,854 --> 00:06:41,062
{\an8}But according to protocol,
you should've taken clearance from DRDO.

79
00:06:42,771 --> 00:06:44,854
Do you know the meaning
of top secret, madam?

80
00:06:48,146 --> 00:06:49,853
"Strictly need-to-know basis."

81
00:06:49,854 --> 00:06:52,145
Understand what science means,
Col. Lakhawat?

82
00:06:52,146 --> 00:06:53,853
Or do you ignore it, too?

83
00:06:53,854 --> 00:06:55,729
You're the one who ignored it, madam.

84
00:06:56,312 --> 00:06:58,104
{\an8}You didn't look carefully.

85
00:06:59,479 --> 00:07:02,896
The Chief Scientist in this program
is your senior

86
00:07:03,104 --> 00:07:05,021
in experience and qualification.

87
00:07:06,187 --> 00:07:07,562
Doctor John Verghese.

88
00:07:09,312 --> 00:07:10,271
Hello, everyone.

89
00:07:15,854 --> 00:07:16,812
The Alpha serum.

90
00:07:17,771 --> 00:07:22,229
It makes our tissues, muscles, and organs
stronger and more efficient.

91
00:07:22,521 --> 00:07:26,854
It improves vision, hearing,
reflexes, senses, and lungs.

92
00:07:27,771 --> 00:07:29,729
Improves everything.

93
00:07:31,062 --> 00:07:33,562
{\an8}What if a soldier is hit by a bullet?

94
00:07:35,062 --> 00:07:37,687
Soldiers are not invincible.
They're human.

95
00:07:38,396 --> 00:07:41,770
A headshot would kill them.

96
00:07:41,771 --> 00:07:45,687
But if the wound isn't serious,
the Alpha serum can heal it.

97
00:07:46,812 --> 00:07:51,604
In nature, many creatures like lizards
and lobsters can regenerate.

98
00:07:52,229 --> 00:07:56,604
The Alpha serum acts on damaged organs
by mimicking that process.

99
00:07:57,229 --> 00:08:00,146
The initial idea was to facilitate…

100
00:08:01,604 --> 00:08:03,521
faster recovery for our soldiers.

101
00:08:04,021 --> 00:08:08,021
How often must this serum be administered?
Before every mission?

102
00:08:08,271 --> 00:08:09,521
Once you go Alpha,

103
00:08:10,312 --> 00:08:11,562
you can't go back.

104
00:08:13,021 --> 00:08:16,937
We need everyone's approval to
take this program to the next level.

105
00:08:32,479 --> 00:08:34,479
{\an8}Did you talk to Janaki's sister?

106
00:08:34,729 --> 00:08:37,104
She was going to get a second opinion
in Spain.

107
00:08:37,729 --> 00:08:39,271
Yes, I received Aruna's email.

108
00:08:39,479 --> 00:08:40,937
I'm glad we found out in time.

109
00:08:41,062 --> 00:08:42,021
Found out what?

110
00:08:42,979 --> 00:08:46,396
I'm a bloody scientist, Preeti.
I don't believe in luck.

111
00:08:46,812 --> 00:08:49,437
Not in sugar-coating either.
Just give me the facts, please.

112
00:08:50,021 --> 00:08:50,979
It's confirmed.

113
00:08:52,521 --> 00:08:53,937
Congenital heart disease.

114
00:08:57,312 --> 00:09:00,021
During pregnancy, the mother's heart
has to work double.

115
00:09:01,312 --> 00:09:03,187
Your heart can't handle it.

116
00:09:04,312 --> 00:09:06,187
This is suicidal, Janaki.

117
00:09:06,396 --> 00:09:08,729
It's your first trimester.
It's still possible.

118
00:09:09,479 --> 00:09:10,521
You need to have an abortion.

119
00:09:12,771 --> 00:09:14,854
So I can never be a mother?

120
00:09:26,604 --> 00:09:28,187
We don't have a choice, Janaki.

121
00:09:29,396 --> 00:09:30,271
Please.

122
00:09:31,771 --> 00:09:32,979
I'm with you.

123
00:09:33,604 --> 00:09:34,979
We'll face it together.

124
00:09:35,354 --> 00:09:37,021
We've tried for so many years.

125
00:09:37,771 --> 00:09:39,062
It's too much of a risk.

126
00:09:39,687 --> 00:09:42,062
If I feared death,
I would not have married a soldier.

127
00:09:43,021 --> 00:09:46,354
I listened to my heart then,
and I'll listen to it now.

128
00:09:49,104 --> 00:09:50,062
My heart is weak,

129
00:09:53,062 --> 00:09:54,562
but it has made a decision.

130
00:09:55,021 --> 00:09:56,354
Why are you so stubborn?

131
00:09:58,646 --> 00:10:00,896
Stubborn girls change the world, Vikrant.

132
00:10:02,854 --> 00:10:04,979
This child has chosen us.

133
00:10:07,729 --> 00:10:09,229
We're having this baby.

134
00:10:10,687 --> 00:10:11,604
Promise me?

135
00:10:20,062 --> 00:10:21,854
<i>Your heart can't handle it.</i>

136
00:10:22,604 --> 00:10:26,270
<i>My heart is weak,
but it has made a decision.</i>

137
00:10:26,271 --> 00:10:30,604
<i>It makes our tissues, muscles, and organs
stronger and more efficient.</i>

138
00:10:31,937 --> 00:10:34,729
{\an8}<i>The Alpha serum repairs
damaged organs.</i>

139
00:10:37,187 --> 00:10:38,646
{\an8}<i>We're having this baby.</i>

140
00:10:41,854 --> 00:10:42,854
{\an8}<i>Promise me?</i>

141
00:10:50,146 --> 00:10:51,479
This is a medical miracle.

142
00:10:52,229 --> 00:10:53,771
Janaki's heart is improving.

143
00:10:53,979 --> 00:10:57,104
It's showing rapid improvement.
And no complications with the pregnancy.

144
00:10:58,229 --> 00:11:00,229
Janaki, it's the last two months.

145
00:11:00,437 --> 00:11:01,396
So take care, okay?

146
00:11:02,854 --> 00:11:03,771
Thank you.

147
00:11:09,396 --> 00:11:10,312
Come.

148
00:11:19,437 --> 00:11:20,979
Our Alpha soldiers.

149
00:11:24,354 --> 00:11:25,312
Brain hemorrhage.

150
00:11:26,604 --> 00:11:29,312
Three of the six died on the spot
from a brain bleed.

151
00:11:30,687 --> 00:11:32,312
The other three are in the ICU.

152
00:11:33,396 --> 00:11:35,979
According to the program,
my team has been

153
00:11:36,729 --> 00:11:39,729
monitoring their vitals for the past
ten months. Every day.

154
00:11:41,146 --> 00:11:44,146
Their vitals were perfect.
There was no warning.

155
00:11:45,062 --> 00:11:47,979
- Sir, you know why this happened, right?
- Alpha.

156
00:11:57,854 --> 00:11:58,771
Move!

157
00:12:22,854 --> 00:12:24,854
<i>We're trying to save the child.</i>

158
00:12:29,479 --> 00:12:30,521
Guru <i>ji.</i>

159
00:12:30,854 --> 00:12:33,187
Did you give the Alpha serum to Janaki?

160
00:12:39,062 --> 00:12:42,603
{\an8}I thought I would save her.

161
00:12:42,604 --> 00:12:45,937
{\an8}You didn't save her. You killed her!

162
00:12:48,812 --> 00:12:51,646
{\an8}Alpha is the property
of the Indian Government.

163
00:12:52,312 --> 00:12:56,146
It was only tried on soldiers,
who signed up for it.

164
00:12:56,521 --> 00:12:57,896
{\an8}Do you understand what this means?

165
00:13:01,062 --> 00:13:04,812
{\an8}The Alpha serum is running
through your child's veins.

166
00:13:05,896 --> 00:13:08,062
Your baby belongs to the country.

167
00:13:08,521 --> 00:13:11,312
{\an8}Only the country has rights
over the child, not you.

168
00:13:16,562 --> 00:13:17,437
Vikrant.

169
00:13:20,312 --> 00:13:21,187
I'm sorry.

170
00:13:21,687 --> 00:13:23,187
We couldn't save Janaki.

171
00:13:36,271 --> 00:13:37,312
Take the baby away.

172
00:13:50,271 --> 00:13:51,229
Vikrant!

173
00:13:52,479 --> 00:13:53,646
Vikrant! Listen to me.

174
00:13:55,396 --> 00:13:56,812
They've taken your daughter.

175
00:14:07,312 --> 00:14:08,271
Where's my daughter?

176
00:14:15,521 --> 00:14:16,562
She's gone numb.

177
00:14:17,146 --> 00:14:18,229
She's cold.

178
00:14:20,354 --> 00:14:21,812
She's not breathing, Fateh.

179
00:14:22,229 --> 00:14:23,354
She's dead, Guru <i>ji.</i>

180
00:14:29,437 --> 00:14:30,937
You shouldn't have stolen the serum.

181
00:14:32,021 --> 00:14:33,646
{\an8}But I won't let them arrest you.

182
00:14:34,229 --> 00:14:36,437
I respect soldiers like you.

183
00:14:40,687 --> 00:14:41,646
{\an8}I was a soldier.

184
00:14:44,104 --> 00:14:44,979
{\an8}I'm done.

185
00:15:03,771 --> 00:15:05,979
Internal Inquiry has testified that

186
00:15:06,187 --> 00:15:09,978
Alpha should have been tested
for another six months.

187
00:15:09,979 --> 00:15:11,146
But you pushed it.

188
00:15:11,604 --> 00:15:12,812
I did.

189
00:15:13,854 --> 00:15:16,646
Nor did I ask for anyone's permission.

190
00:15:16,937 --> 00:15:18,604
Six cadets are dead.

191
00:15:18,937 --> 00:15:21,021
If this version of Alpha had worked,

192
00:15:21,896 --> 00:15:23,687
how many cadets would've been saved?

193
00:15:24,396 --> 00:15:28,396
What use is blood
if it does not spill for the nation?

194
00:15:28,937 --> 00:15:32,729
A bullet didn't kill them.
Your negligence did.

195
00:15:33,062 --> 00:15:36,061
Disobeying orders is not a mistake.
It's a crime.

196
00:15:36,062 --> 00:15:39,561
Under normal circumstances,
the punishment is court-martial.

197
00:15:39,562 --> 00:15:42,645
But considering your exemplary
career record,

198
00:15:42,646 --> 00:15:46,229
this Committee has decided to take
disciplinary action instead.

199
00:15:46,687 --> 00:15:47,687
We're demoting you.

200
00:15:48,646 --> 00:15:51,354
<i>You'll be demoted from Colonel
to Lt. Colonel.</i>

201
00:15:53,354 --> 00:15:57,187
<i>You're now posted to the Cherrapunji
Special Forces base.</i>

202
00:15:58,979 --> 00:16:02,229
<i>A place where you'll never see
the battlefield again.</i>

203
00:16:08,729 --> 00:16:10,104
And as for the Alpha program,

204
00:16:10,812 --> 00:16:13,062
it has been shut down permanently.

205
00:16:17,104 --> 00:16:18,937
Despite this humiliation

206
00:16:19,896 --> 00:16:21,854
and this injustice,

207
00:16:23,479 --> 00:16:24,979
one thing has not changed.

208
00:16:26,354 --> 00:16:27,896
That I am a patriot.

209
00:16:29,187 --> 00:16:30,687
A true patriot.

210
00:16:32,687 --> 00:16:34,104
Mark my words.

211
00:16:35,312 --> 00:16:36,896
The day will come

212
00:16:38,896 --> 00:16:41,812
when you'll hold up my patriotism
as an example to the world.

213
00:16:45,062 --> 00:16:46,812
You have no idea that

214
00:16:48,146 --> 00:16:51,521
by shutting down Alpha today,

215
00:16:52,729 --> 00:16:55,354
what a grave mistake you've made.

216
00:16:58,271 --> 00:16:59,271
Not a mistake.

217
00:17:01,187 --> 00:17:02,146
A sin.

218
00:17:07,187 --> 00:17:08,187
<i>Jai Hind!</i>

219
00:17:35,271 --> 00:17:37,104
I need money and men.

220
00:17:37,854 --> 00:17:38,812
When can we meet?

221
00:18:09,896 --> 00:18:11,646
<i>Sir, I'm in Rajasthan,</i>

222
00:18:12,354 --> 00:18:14,437
and you're far away in Cherrapunji.

223
00:18:15,104 --> 00:18:17,104
How can we work together?

224
00:18:17,437 --> 00:18:21,521
I've been posted to such
an inconsequential place

225
00:18:22,354 --> 00:18:24,271
where no one watches me.

226
00:18:24,771 --> 00:18:26,354
Even though I'm posted in Cherrapunji,

227
00:18:26,937 --> 00:18:28,771
my full focus will be on our program.

228
00:18:30,771 --> 00:18:33,771
Look! Alpha's new facility.

229
00:18:34,312 --> 00:18:36,187
But how?

230
00:18:37,021 --> 00:18:38,062
There are some people

231
00:18:39,271 --> 00:18:41,687
who understand the importance of Alpha.

232
00:18:42,271 --> 00:18:43,229
Who are they, sir?

233
00:18:43,729 --> 00:18:45,937
A few patriots like me.

234
00:18:46,396 --> 00:18:47,729
This was their factory.

235
00:18:48,437 --> 00:18:49,896
Put all your focus on Alpha.

236
00:18:51,312 --> 00:18:52,729
Create a version of the serum

237
00:18:53,437 --> 00:18:56,396
that can be given to every Indian soldier.

238
00:18:57,021 --> 00:18:58,854
Sir, you never give up, do you?

239
00:19:00,021 --> 00:19:01,021
Why would I?

240
00:19:01,479 --> 00:19:04,604
Especially now that
I hold the ace in the pack.

241
00:19:12,771 --> 00:19:15,228
Sir, giving Col. Kaul a stillborn baby
that belonged to someone else

242
00:19:15,229 --> 00:19:18,187
and telling him it was his daughter
was wrong.

243
00:19:18,854 --> 00:19:21,979
Sometimes the line between
right and wrong is blurred, Verghese.

244
00:19:22,729 --> 00:19:26,062
And for me,
nothing matters more than Alpha.

245
00:19:30,937 --> 00:19:32,437
What should we call her, sir?

246
00:19:33,021 --> 00:19:35,062
Her mother's name was Janaki.

247
00:19:37,104 --> 00:19:38,229
We'll call her…

248
00:19:40,521 --> 00:19:41,896
Sita.

249
00:20:03,396 --> 00:20:06,895
{\an8}The baby elephant is with his family,
who protects him.

250
00:20:06,896 --> 00:20:08,187
{\an8}And my parents?

251
00:20:09,687 --> 00:20:10,604
{\an8}Where are they?

252
00:20:11,979 --> 00:20:13,187
{\an8}They abandoned you.

253
00:20:14,437 --> 00:20:15,937
{\an8}Fateh sir brought you here.

254
00:20:28,937 --> 00:20:29,979
{\an8}Verghese Uncle!

255
00:20:31,271 --> 00:20:33,479
<i>Verghese, is the effect
of Alpha showing?</i>

256
00:20:34,187 --> 00:20:35,271
{\an8}<i>Not yet, sir.</i>

257
00:20:50,104 --> 00:20:51,729
{\an8}Happy 12th birthday, Sita!

258
00:20:51,979 --> 00:20:53,604
Uncle, didn't Fateh sir come?

259
00:20:54,187 --> 00:20:56,979
He's very busy.
Otherwise, he'd be here.

260
00:20:58,229 --> 00:20:59,729
Wait. One minute.

261
00:21:01,896 --> 00:21:03,437
{\an8}This is your birthday gift.

262
00:21:04,437 --> 00:21:05,312
{\an8}Wow!

263
00:21:06,979 --> 00:21:07,896
Soldier!

264
00:21:20,396 --> 00:21:22,687
{\an8}<i>Coding and hacking.
She's excellent at both, sir.</i>

265
00:21:23,729 --> 00:21:25,562
{\an8}Way beyond her age.

266
00:21:26,187 --> 00:21:27,728
{\an8}Her IQ is very high, sir.

267
00:21:27,729 --> 00:21:29,312
{\an8}We don't need her to write a book.

268
00:21:30,354 --> 00:21:32,354
{\an8}Tell me, has Alpha shown its effect?

269
00:22:07,896 --> 00:22:09,521
<i>It's the puberty hormone.</i>

270
00:22:10,146 --> 00:22:11,646
{\an8}Alpha has finally kicked in.

271
00:22:12,437 --> 00:22:14,979
{\an8}Through Sita, we'll be able
to develop a new version of Alpha.

272
00:22:29,854 --> 00:22:31,771
{\an8}Are you crying? I see tears.

273
00:22:32,229 --> 00:22:33,146
{\an8}Don't cry.

274
00:22:33,687 --> 00:22:37,937
{\an8}People are either strong or weak.
Gender has nothing to do with it.

275
00:22:39,437 --> 00:22:41,979
{\an8}<i>There are two kinds of people
in this world.</i>

276
00:22:42,271 --> 00:22:43,979
{\an8}<i>Wolves and sheep.</i>

277
00:22:44,437 --> 00:22:45,396
{\an8}I'm a wolf.

278
00:22:46,896 --> 00:22:47,771
{\an8}What are you?

279
00:22:47,896 --> 00:22:49,437
{\an8}A wolf's child is a wolf, sir.

280
00:22:55,312 --> 00:22:56,229
{\an8}<i>Well done!</i>

281
00:22:56,687 --> 00:22:57,687
{\an8}Here's your reward.

282
00:23:00,229 --> 00:23:02,353
{\an8}What did you call your father?

283
00:23:02,354 --> 00:23:03,229
{\an8}Baba.

284
00:23:04,312 --> 00:23:05,187
{\an8}Baba.

285
00:23:08,021 --> 00:23:09,937
I got it for my first mission.

286
00:23:10,604 --> 00:23:12,479
{\an8}When will I get my first mission?

287
00:23:13,437 --> 00:23:15,479
{\an8}When you become an Indian soldier.

288
00:23:21,646 --> 00:23:22,687
What's this?

289
00:23:23,854 --> 00:23:24,729
Alpha.

290
00:23:25,687 --> 00:23:26,729
What's Alpha?

291
00:23:26,979 --> 00:23:29,146
The first letter of the Greek alphabet,

292
00:23:29,604 --> 00:23:31,312
and our program's motto.

293
00:23:32,187 --> 00:23:33,354
The first.

294
00:23:33,521 --> 00:23:34,812
The fastest.

295
00:23:35,229 --> 00:23:36,354
The strongest.

296
00:23:37,854 --> 00:23:40,312
If you look closely, every city
is an urban jungle,

297
00:23:41,146 --> 00:23:43,895
and in that jungle, Alpha rules.

298
00:23:43,896 --> 00:23:48,479
That's why I called the serum "Alpha."
And that's what you are.

299
00:23:49,396 --> 00:23:50,271
Alpha.

300
00:24:20,354 --> 00:24:21,353
{\an8}Sir!

301
00:24:21,354 --> 00:24:24,103
{\an8}Sir, it's Tel Aviv. The Mossad Chief
wants a word.

302
00:24:24,104 --> 00:24:26,936
{\an8}- Cancel everything. This takes priority.
- Yes, sir.

303
00:24:26,937 --> 00:24:27,812
Let's get to it.

304
00:24:28,104 --> 00:24:29,353
- Karan.
- Yes, sir.

305
00:24:29,354 --> 00:24:30,687
- Show me.
- Sir.

306
00:24:32,229 --> 00:24:33,437
Sir, five bodies were found.

307
00:24:33,854 --> 00:24:35,687
The first was Subrato Das.

308
00:24:36,312 --> 00:24:37,687
<i>He was traveling alone
in the last metro.</i>

309
00:24:40,437 --> 00:24:42,104
<i>Just one stab. Dead.</i>

310
00:24:43,437 --> 00:24:45,479
<i>Five hours later, Amit Thakur.</i>

311
00:24:46,271 --> 00:24:48,187
{\an8}<i>He saw someone ahead,
so he honked.</i>

312
00:24:49,979 --> 00:24:50,979
<i>The car was rigged.</i>

313
00:24:52,021 --> 00:24:54,896
Number three, Ajinkya Sethi.
A sniper kill, sir.

314
00:24:55,187 --> 00:24:58,771
The bullet went through the window and
his glasses, straight into his left eye.

315
00:25:00,812 --> 00:25:02,187
Next was Madhur Kulkarni.

316
00:25:03,479 --> 00:25:04,687
<i>In broad daylight, a headshot.</i>

317
00:25:05,729 --> 00:25:06,729
<i>Fearless.</i>

318
00:25:09,187 --> 00:25:12,646
The last and most ruthless, Susan Cherian.

319
00:25:18,521 --> 00:25:19,854
<i>Suffocated to death.</i>

320
00:25:22,646 --> 00:25:24,812
Sir, they've all been murdered
in the past 48 hours.

321
00:25:25,062 --> 00:25:27,354
All from different departments
and ministries.

322
00:25:27,604 --> 00:25:29,520
DRDO, NSA, NSG,

323
00:25:29,521 --> 00:25:31,936
Military Intelligence,
and the Ministry of Defense.

324
00:25:31,937 --> 00:25:36,021
We're trying to work out the common link
that made them targets.

325
00:25:44,687 --> 00:25:45,604
Alpha.

326
00:25:58,646 --> 00:26:01,562
ID Sita. 14:25 hours.

327
00:26:02,312 --> 00:26:03,271
Access granted.

328
00:26:31,896 --> 00:26:32,937
Where were you for the last two days?

329
00:26:35,521 --> 00:26:36,521
What are you eating?

330
00:26:39,896 --> 00:26:40,812
Thanks.

331
00:26:41,562 --> 00:26:42,521
I haven't had breakfast.

332
00:26:46,854 --> 00:26:47,771
So…

333
00:27:09,979 --> 00:27:11,604
Sita, what are you doing?

334
00:27:28,646 --> 00:27:29,687
Good morning, Baba.

335
00:27:31,271 --> 00:27:33,896
{\an8}Today Sita herself has come
to burn Lanka.

336
00:27:47,604 --> 00:27:48,728
<i>Sita has gone crazy!</i>

337
00:27:48,729 --> 00:27:50,729
<i>She's killing everyone. Find her.</i>

338
00:27:54,687 --> 00:27:56,937
<i>Let's get her! Get the bombs!
Get the guns!</i>

339
00:28:09,771 --> 00:28:10,729
Grenade!

340
00:28:33,187 --> 00:28:34,062
Hi, boys.

341
00:29:30,396 --> 00:29:32,187
<i>Where are my parents?</i>

342
00:29:39,354 --> 00:29:40,895
<i>Happy 12th birthday, Sita!</i>

343
00:29:40,896 --> 00:29:42,604
<i>- Uncle, didn't Fateh sir come?
- He's very busy.</i>

344
00:29:44,354 --> 00:29:46,104
<i>I'm a wolf. What are you?</i>

345
00:29:46,437 --> 00:29:47,437
<i>One shot.</i>

346
00:29:47,896 --> 00:29:48,771
<i>One kill!</i>

347
00:29:49,521 --> 00:29:52,312
<i>There's only one punishment
for a traitor.</i>

348
00:29:52,562 --> 00:29:54,104
<i>On your 18th birthday,</i>

349
00:29:54,271 --> 00:29:56,312
<i>what could be more special than that?</i>

350
00:29:57,062 --> 00:29:58,062
<i>One kill!</i>

351
00:31:54,646 --> 00:31:56,604
<i>Target in sight! Target in sight!</i>

352
00:31:56,729 --> 00:31:57,896
<i>Sita is on the bridge.</i>

353
00:31:58,021 --> 00:32:01,062
<i>Don't lose visual. I repeat.
Do not lose the visual.</i>

354
00:32:01,562 --> 00:32:02,729
<i>No one will shoot!</i>

355
00:32:05,396 --> 00:32:06,646
Have you lost it?

356
00:32:07,062 --> 00:32:08,104
Hands up, Sita!

357
00:32:08,646 --> 00:32:09,812
Drop the gun!

358
00:32:11,354 --> 00:32:12,396
Put the gun down!

359
00:34:23,229 --> 00:34:28,562
Why did R&AW Chief Vikrant Kaul travel
to a remote corner of the country

360
00:34:28,896 --> 00:34:30,562
to meet a forgotten soldier?

361
00:34:35,021 --> 00:34:36,104
I had no choice.

362
00:34:37,854 --> 00:34:42,062
Honestly, Guru <i>ji,</i> stay out of this.
It's in your best interest.

363
00:34:42,479 --> 00:34:43,604
What are you up to, Fateh?

364
00:35:06,896 --> 00:35:07,896
{\an8}<i>I've killed six.</i>

365
00:35:08,771 --> 00:35:09,687
{\an8}<i>Now just two left.</i>

366
00:35:16,979 --> 00:35:17,896
Who is she?

367
00:35:18,229 --> 00:35:19,187
How did you get this?

368
00:35:22,312 --> 00:35:25,854
Look carefully. You know her.

369
00:35:26,187 --> 00:35:27,771
She's very close to you.

370
00:35:39,854 --> 00:35:41,937
I buried my daughter
with my own two hands.

371
00:35:43,146 --> 00:35:44,146
Sita.

372
00:35:45,729 --> 00:35:47,229
Her name is Sita.

373
00:35:58,021 --> 00:36:00,896
Sita became the Alpha soldier
we all hoped for.

374
00:36:01,521 --> 00:36:04,312
She was my pride. Our very best.

375
00:36:04,979 --> 00:36:06,604
Then one day she flipped.

376
00:36:07,062 --> 00:36:08,896
The serum twisted her brain.

377
00:36:09,479 --> 00:36:11,437
Everyone associated with the program…

378
00:36:12,562 --> 00:36:13,937
she's killing them all.

379
00:36:14,562 --> 00:36:17,521
Special Forces shut Alpha down
twenty years ago.

380
00:36:18,562 --> 00:36:19,812
How are you running it?

381
00:36:20,729 --> 00:36:22,896
Who is funding it?

382
00:36:25,646 --> 00:36:27,354
I never thought you'd become a traitor!

383
00:36:27,854 --> 00:36:29,812
Sita is the traitor, Guru <i>ji.</i>

384
00:36:30,229 --> 00:36:32,228
She's killing our national assets.

385
00:36:32,229 --> 00:36:35,562
Now she's after the R&AW Chief
and a Lt. Colonel.

386
00:36:36,229 --> 00:36:37,396
Don't worry.

387
00:36:37,687 --> 00:36:39,062
My men are looking for her.

388
00:36:39,479 --> 00:36:41,853
When they find her, they'll kill her.

389
00:36:41,854 --> 00:36:43,062
She's my daughter, Fateh.

390
00:36:43,437 --> 00:36:46,312
How? You don't even know her.

391
00:36:47,062 --> 00:36:51,396
You can't imagine how hard
it is for me to kill her.

392
00:36:52,604 --> 00:36:55,062
Your daughter died twenty years ago.

393
00:36:55,812 --> 00:36:57,354
Now she's my Sita.

394
00:36:59,729 --> 00:37:01,812
I'll expose the truth
about you to everyone,

395
00:37:02,479 --> 00:37:03,854
and you'll hang for it.

396
00:37:05,729 --> 00:37:06,687
I will.

397
00:37:09,187 --> 00:37:10,646
But only after Sita.

398
00:37:11,646 --> 00:37:14,062
After all, she's the one murdering people.

399
00:37:14,729 --> 00:37:17,729
Don't let your emotions cloud
your judgment again, Guru <i>ji.</i>

400
00:37:18,812 --> 00:37:20,604
The last time you did that,

401
00:37:21,687 --> 00:37:23,021
you lost your wife.

402
00:37:24,187 --> 00:37:25,854
This time it may be your daughter.

403
00:37:55,812 --> 00:37:56,854
I hate coffee.

404
00:37:58,187 --> 00:38:00,062
Baba gave me the habit, Soldier.

405
00:38:00,396 --> 00:38:02,062
One cup for him,

406
00:38:03,146 --> 00:38:04,062
and one for me.

407
00:38:05,062 --> 00:38:06,729
I'll have my last cup with him.

408
00:38:10,604 --> 00:38:12,271
I'll get our revenge, Soldier.

409
00:38:13,229 --> 00:38:14,771
Two lab rats have survived.

410
00:38:15,104 --> 00:38:16,812
But we'll kill Baba at the very end.

411
00:38:17,437 --> 00:38:19,021
Like enjoying a fine dessert
after lunch.

412
00:38:23,062 --> 00:38:24,521
We'll save the best for the last.

413
00:38:26,646 --> 00:38:29,312
But before that… Vikrant Kaul.

414
00:38:31,771 --> 00:38:34,021
Kaul. A Kashmiri Pandit surname.

415
00:38:34,229 --> 00:38:36,271
Sanskrit for "family."

416
00:38:37,646 --> 00:38:40,520
He left the army 20 years ago.
Then he went totally off the grid.

417
00:38:40,521 --> 00:38:43,896
After Luthra died, he was
suddenly appointed R&AW Chief.

418
00:38:44,312 --> 00:38:46,229
Congratulations, Vikrant!

419
00:38:51,687 --> 00:38:52,604
I love it.

420
00:39:01,104 --> 00:39:02,146
Okay.

421
00:39:02,604 --> 00:39:06,271
Two weeks ago, he flew from Delhi
to Madrid, from there to Valladolid.

422
00:39:06,812 --> 00:39:09,811
Four days later, he came back to India
from Spain.

423
00:39:09,812 --> 00:39:14,229
The same route last month.
In March too. And in December.

424
00:39:15,729 --> 00:39:17,437
These R&AW guys love travelling!

425
00:39:18,187 --> 00:39:19,437
He's in Spain again?

426
00:39:20,896 --> 00:39:21,812
Sad.

427
00:39:23,187 --> 00:39:25,187
We'll have to wait
till he's back in India.

428
00:39:33,271 --> 00:39:35,687
Soldier, all his trips to Spain
were on commercial flights.

429
00:39:36,812 --> 00:39:38,146
That means personal trips.

430
00:39:41,771 --> 00:39:43,646
What's special about Spain, Kaul?

431
00:40:11,437 --> 00:40:13,354
<i>Girl's got style!</i>

432
00:40:14,104 --> 00:40:16,187
<i>A firecracker</i>

433
00:40:16,521 --> 00:40:17,646
<i>No touching</i>

434
00:40:18,646 --> 00:40:20,978
<i>Lightning striking</i>

435
00:40:20,979 --> 00:40:22,354
<i>Girl's a storm</i>

436
00:40:23,354 --> 00:40:25,354
<i>Challenge her</i>

437
00:40:25,687 --> 00:40:26,979
<i>You've had it</i>

438
00:40:27,812 --> 00:40:29,896
<i>Acts first</i>

439
00:40:30,146 --> 00:40:31,479
<i>Thinks later</i>

440
00:40:32,771 --> 00:40:34,854
<i>Kohl-lined eyes</i>

441
00:40:35,021 --> 00:40:37,104
<i>Burning through the heart</i>

442
00:40:37,312 --> 00:40:40,562
<i>Encircles the heart
Now she's gone</i>

443
00:40:40,812 --> 00:40:43,061
<i>Girl's chilled Champagne</i>

444
00:40:43,062 --> 00:40:45,353
<i>Toned and maintained</i>

445
00:40:45,354 --> 00:40:47,812
<i>Cast off the evil eye</i>

446
00:40:47,937 --> 00:40:49,978
<i>Girl's got style!</i>

447
00:40:49,979 --> 00:40:52,145
<i>Girl's chilled Champagne</i>

448
00:40:52,146 --> 00:40:54,354
<i>Toned and maintained</i>

449
00:40:54,521 --> 00:40:56,936
<i>Cast off the evil eye</i>

450
00:40:56,937 --> 00:40:58,979
<i>Girl's got style!</i>

451
00:40:59,937 --> 00:41:01,979
<i>Soft breeze</i>

452
00:41:02,187 --> 00:41:04,396
<i>Wind perplexed</i>

453
00:41:04,521 --> 00:41:06,521
<i>Sturdy form</i>

454
00:41:06,771 --> 00:41:07,896
<i>Kickass</i>

455
00:41:08,021 --> 00:41:09,103
<i>Kickass</i>

456
00:41:09,104 --> 00:41:11,062
<i>Challenge her</i>

457
00:41:11,354 --> 00:41:13,562
<i>You've had it</i>

458
00:41:13,687 --> 00:41:15,562
<i>Acts first</i>

459
00:41:16,021 --> 00:41:17,062
<i>Thinks later</i>

460
00:41:40,646 --> 00:41:42,853
<i>Those eyes of hers</i>

461
00:41:42,854 --> 00:41:45,229
<i>Robs the whole village</i>

462
00:41:45,437 --> 00:41:47,686
<i>She heeds no one</i>

463
00:41:47,687 --> 00:41:49,478
<i>Her law is law</i>

464
00:41:49,479 --> 00:41:51,686
<i>Sweet as honey</i>

465
00:41:51,687 --> 00:41:53,936
<i>Melting in the mouth</i>

466
00:41:53,937 --> 00:41:56,853
<i>Showers colors</i>

467
00:41:56,854 --> 00:41:58,645
<i>To the world</i>

468
00:41:58,646 --> 00:42:00,686
<i>Girl's chilled Champagne</i>

469
00:42:00,687 --> 00:42:03,020
<i>Toned and maintained</i>

470
00:42:03,021 --> 00:42:05,686
<i>Cast off the evil eye</i>

471
00:42:05,687 --> 00:42:07,770
<i>Girl's got style!</i>

472
00:42:07,771 --> 00:42:09,853
<i>Girl's chilled Champagne</i>

473
00:42:09,854 --> 00:42:12,103
<i>Toned and maintained</i>

474
00:42:12,104 --> 00:42:14,562
<i>Cast off the evil eye</i>

475
00:42:14,771 --> 00:42:16,854
<i>Girl's got style!</i>

476
00:42:17,604 --> 00:42:19,562
<i>A firecracker</i>

477
00:42:19,896 --> 00:42:21,229
<i>No touching</i>

478
00:42:22,229 --> 00:42:24,146
<i>Lightning striking</i>

479
00:42:24,521 --> 00:42:25,729
<i>Girl's a storm</i>

480
00:42:26,937 --> 00:42:28,771
<i>Challenge her</i>

481
00:42:29,062 --> 00:42:30,354
<i>You've had it</i>

482
00:42:30,521 --> 00:42:33,311
<i>- Cast off the evil eye
- Acts first</i>

483
00:42:33,312 --> 00:42:35,021
<i>Girl's got style!</i>

484
00:43:06,062 --> 00:43:07,062
<i>Vikrant, listen to me.</i>

485
00:43:08,771 --> 00:43:10,229
{\an8}They've taken your daughter.

486
00:43:10,896 --> 00:43:13,062
{\an8}No, listen! I want to show you something.

487
00:43:13,396 --> 00:43:14,937
{\an8}Just come. Just come with me.

488
00:43:15,354 --> 00:43:17,187
I overheard Colonel Fateh.

489
00:43:17,437 --> 00:43:21,062
{\an8}The Alpha serum is running
through your child's veins.

490
00:43:21,646 --> 00:43:23,729
Your baby belongs to the country.

491
00:43:25,104 --> 00:43:26,229
Your other daughter.

492
00:43:28,396 --> 00:43:30,604
- What?
- I'm sorry, Vikrant.

493
00:43:30,854 --> 00:43:34,354
{\an8}Janaki knew, but she didn't tell you.
She also stopped me from telling you.

494
00:43:36,062 --> 00:43:37,479
Having one baby was a risk,

495
00:43:38,229 --> 00:43:41,312
and she knew you'd never let her
carry two babies.

496
00:43:42,562 --> 00:43:45,187
They're twins, but not identical.

497
00:43:46,062 --> 00:43:48,354
The sister, who was born first,
protected the other.

498
00:43:49,937 --> 00:43:53,436
No one must know about this.
And please--

499
00:43:53,437 --> 00:43:54,729
I'll delete all the records.

500
00:43:59,979 --> 00:44:02,479
<i>Thanks, Aruna, for bringing her here.</i>

501
00:44:02,896 --> 00:44:05,271
Vikrant, how will you live without her?

502
00:44:06,437 --> 00:44:07,729
She's our niece.

503
00:44:08,437 --> 00:44:09,979
We'll be more than happy
to have her, but…

504
00:44:10,646 --> 00:44:11,687
you're her father.

505
00:44:12,312 --> 00:44:14,229
I have no option, Manish.

506
00:44:14,937 --> 00:44:16,812
No one must know she's my daughter.

507
00:44:18,646 --> 00:44:20,271
I want her to lead a normal life.

508
00:44:20,437 --> 00:44:23,229
When she's older and starts
asking questions…

509
00:44:24,229 --> 00:44:25,271
I'll tell her the truth

510
00:44:27,479 --> 00:44:29,479
about what happened
to her mother and sister.

511
00:44:32,354 --> 00:44:33,937
Thought of a name for her?

512
00:44:34,521 --> 00:44:35,812
You know Janaki loved this name…

513
00:44:37,771 --> 00:44:38,729
Durga.

514
00:44:40,521 --> 00:44:43,687
The destroyer of demons. Durga.

515
00:44:45,521 --> 00:44:47,562
I always said you were special.

516
00:44:48,062 --> 00:44:49,562
There was no one like you.

517
00:44:50,604 --> 00:44:51,604
But there is someone, Durga.

518
00:44:52,479 --> 00:44:53,604
She's just like you.

519
00:44:57,854 --> 00:45:00,854
<i>This is Mom, this is you,
and this is my sister.</i>

520
00:45:01,062 --> 00:45:02,521
<i>And I'm the one behind her.</i>

521
00:45:02,979 --> 00:45:04,812
<i>She always protected me.</i>

522
00:45:05,396 --> 00:45:07,771
Pa, did you think of a name for her?

523
00:45:16,271 --> 00:45:17,312
Si…

524
00:45:18,812 --> 00:45:19,812
Sita?

525
00:45:22,187 --> 00:45:24,104
- Is she okay?
- She's in terrible danger.

526
00:45:27,021 --> 00:45:28,562
Fateh will kill her.

527
00:45:30,187 --> 00:45:31,229
Or she'll kill Fateh.

528
00:45:33,521 --> 00:45:34,521
And you too.

529
00:45:35,646 --> 00:45:37,729
To be honest, she should kill me.

530
00:45:38,021 --> 00:45:39,811
Because I've been
a horrible father to her.

531
00:45:39,812 --> 00:45:41,396
What? No, no, no.
Pa, listen to me.

532
00:45:42,021 --> 00:45:43,479
You're the best father in the world.

533
00:45:44,604 --> 00:45:46,812
When you got the chance,
you did your best.

534
00:45:48,062 --> 00:45:49,646
What happened was not your fault.

535
00:45:52,521 --> 00:45:53,604
I need your help.

536
00:45:55,979 --> 00:45:57,187
We need to find her.

537
00:45:57,812 --> 00:45:59,854
We have to save her at any cost.

538
00:46:02,312 --> 00:46:03,479
If Sita is caught,

539
00:46:04,604 --> 00:46:06,896
she'll be arrested for the murders.

540
00:46:07,521 --> 00:46:09,937
As the R&AW Chief,
I can't protect her officially.

541
00:46:11,312 --> 00:46:12,687
We have to do it unofficially.

542
00:46:13,562 --> 00:46:15,437
Only you and me.

543
00:46:16,062 --> 00:46:18,854
For Sita. For our family.

544
00:46:19,396 --> 00:46:21,437
Maybe I trained you for this day.

545
00:46:27,729 --> 00:46:33,021
Pa, not a day has gone by that
I haven't missed my sister, Sita.

546
00:46:34,854 --> 00:46:37,354
She was born first
so she could protect me.

547
00:46:38,354 --> 00:46:41,021
I've always wondered
how I'd ever repay her.

548
00:46:43,729 --> 00:46:45,271
I guess this is my only chance.

549
00:46:47,521 --> 00:46:49,021
Let's bring Sita home, Pa.

550
00:46:51,271 --> 00:46:53,062
Let's make our family a family again.

551
00:47:01,271 --> 00:47:02,312
We got him, Soldier!

552
00:47:05,312 --> 00:47:08,104
Yes! Mr. Family Man
is coming back to India.

553
00:47:08,479 --> 00:47:12,312
Spain Air 5837A. Madrid to Delhi,
Delhi to Srinagar.

554
00:47:13,021 --> 00:47:14,771
Srinagar? Kashmir?

555
00:47:15,479 --> 00:47:16,479
Why Kashmir?

556
00:47:23,979 --> 00:47:24,979
Come on, Sita!

557
00:47:25,854 --> 00:47:28,187
He's Kashmiri. Of course
he'd have a home in Kashmir.

558
00:47:28,646 --> 00:47:31,812
Vikrant Kaul,
property registrations? Nothing.

559
00:47:36,812 --> 00:47:37,936
<i>Any other family member?</i>

560
00:47:37,937 --> 00:47:39,479
<i>Janaki Kaul. Wife.</i>

561
00:47:43,812 --> 00:47:44,687
Boom!

562
00:47:48,562 --> 00:47:49,812
Nicely done, Janaki.

563
00:47:50,479 --> 00:47:52,104
Such a huge house in Betaab Valley!

564
00:48:16,104 --> 00:48:17,021
Cool.

565
00:48:37,562 --> 00:48:38,437
Pretty.

566
00:49:07,187 --> 00:49:08,521
Was it necessary to travel separately?

567
00:49:08,812 --> 00:49:10,687
<i>It's for your own safety, kiddo.</i>

568
00:49:10,979 --> 00:49:12,854
Being careful is the new brave.

569
00:49:13,979 --> 00:49:16,396
That's quite cool. Just like this house.

570
00:49:18,771 --> 00:49:21,771
Wow, Pa! Ma had some great taste.

571
00:49:21,896 --> 00:49:23,729
This is so beautiful!

572
00:49:24,187 --> 00:49:27,478
This place has been my off-grid
personal base for years.

573
00:49:27,479 --> 00:49:29,104
<i>It's my own safe house.</i>

574
00:49:29,562 --> 00:49:31,896
The kitchen is completely stocked up.

575
00:49:32,146 --> 00:49:34,104
Your favorite Italian coffee
is there too.

576
00:49:35,021 --> 00:49:35,896
Coffee.

577
00:49:36,062 --> 00:49:37,354
I'll get there ASAP.

578
00:49:37,479 --> 00:49:38,562
<i>Okay. See you, Pa.</i>

579
00:49:38,771 --> 00:49:39,979
- Love you.
- Love you.

580
00:50:19,354 --> 00:50:20,229
Cool.

581
00:51:46,021 --> 00:51:47,104
Sita?

582
00:51:48,229 --> 00:51:49,937
Fateh sent you for me?

583
00:51:53,021 --> 00:51:54,104
He has hurt my ego.

584
00:51:55,396 --> 00:51:57,729
No, no, no. I'm so sorry.
I didn't know.

585
00:51:57,937 --> 00:51:59,271
I'm your sister.

586
00:52:01,687 --> 00:52:02,604
Sister?

587
00:52:04,021 --> 00:52:04,979
Should I tie you a <i>rakhi?</i>

588
00:52:25,271 --> 00:52:26,229
Sita.

589
00:52:28,396 --> 00:52:31,229
I just want to talk to you. Please.

590
00:52:31,812 --> 00:52:32,812
The rule is simple.

591
00:52:33,354 --> 00:52:35,896
If you can stop me, then you get to talk.

592
00:52:46,937 --> 00:52:47,937
Can we talk now?

593
00:53:05,271 --> 00:53:06,271
Still wanna talk?

594
00:54:21,646 --> 00:54:22,979
So you wanna sit and talk?

595
00:54:24,229 --> 00:54:25,146
Okay.

596
00:54:27,604 --> 00:54:28,896
You shouldn't have laughed.

597
00:55:01,979 --> 00:55:04,729
Sita… that's our father.

598
00:55:23,062 --> 00:55:23,979
Sita.

599
00:55:25,896 --> 00:55:26,854
Papa.

600
00:55:36,604 --> 00:55:37,479
Pa!

601
00:55:46,896 --> 00:55:47,979
We don't look alike.

602
00:56:13,437 --> 00:56:14,312
Want some?

603
00:56:15,354 --> 00:56:16,646
You've gotten plenty of cardio too.

604
00:56:17,937 --> 00:56:18,812
Don't eat.

605
00:56:19,104 --> 00:56:20,896
I'm just loving this <i>desi</i> Chinese.

606
00:56:22,937 --> 00:56:23,812
I…

607
00:56:24,479 --> 00:56:25,729
I'm so sorry, kiddo.

608
00:56:29,229 --> 00:56:30,146
"Kiddo"?

609
00:56:32,146 --> 00:56:33,479
Don't get ahead of yourself, Kaul.

610
00:56:34,687 --> 00:56:35,604
And you?

611
00:56:35,896 --> 00:56:36,937
What nonsense were you saying?

612
00:56:38,187 --> 00:56:40,687
That we're sisters?
And he's our father?

613
00:56:41,187 --> 00:56:42,187
That's the truth.

614
00:56:42,437 --> 00:56:43,312
Shut up!

615
00:56:47,604 --> 00:56:48,479
Who is she?

616
00:56:50,312 --> 00:56:51,187
My mother?

617
00:56:51,562 --> 00:56:53,521
Yes. Janaki.

618
00:56:54,479 --> 00:56:56,437
- Didn't she come on the family vacation?
- She died…

619
00:56:57,271 --> 00:56:58,771
after giving birth to you both.

620
00:57:03,021 --> 00:57:03,896
Sita…

621
00:57:06,396 --> 00:57:09,229
you and I are twins.
I'm exactly like you.

622
00:57:11,229 --> 00:57:12,729
Look, sis, you're good.

623
00:57:13,146 --> 00:57:14,771
It's been a while since
anyone challenged me.

624
00:57:16,937 --> 00:57:18,354
But exactly like me?

625
00:57:27,896 --> 00:57:29,104
Who are these two boring people?

626
00:57:29,729 --> 00:57:30,646
My parents.

627
00:57:31,354 --> 00:57:32,896
I mean, my adoptive parents.

628
00:57:35,729 --> 00:57:38,021
Adoptive parents?

629
00:57:46,271 --> 00:57:47,687
How many parents does she have?

630
00:57:47,812 --> 00:57:48,729
Listen to me--

631
00:57:56,979 --> 00:58:00,104
She has three parents here
and one in heaven.

632
00:58:01,396 --> 00:58:02,562
And what did I get?

633
00:58:04,604 --> 00:58:05,479
Fateh.

634
00:58:07,979 --> 00:58:09,854
What's the difference between
a guinea pig and me?

635
00:58:13,104 --> 00:58:17,354
What is the difference between
a guinea pig and me, Kaul?

636
00:58:22,062 --> 00:58:25,145
After a few days of experiments,
the guinea pig

637
00:58:25,146 --> 00:58:27,562
is put down using sodium pentobarbital.

638
00:58:29,979 --> 00:58:32,562
And me? I didn't even get that option.

639
00:58:38,854 --> 00:58:41,312
Sita, Fateh lied to Pa.

640
00:58:41,937 --> 00:58:43,854
Pa thought you were dead all this time.

641
00:58:45,104 --> 00:58:46,437
If I'd known about you,

642
00:58:46,729 --> 00:58:49,811
none of this would've happened.
I'd have come to save you.

643
00:58:49,812 --> 00:58:50,771
Like you've come today?

644
00:59:01,104 --> 00:59:02,021
What is it, sis?

645
00:59:03,479 --> 00:59:04,562
Feeling bad for me?

646
00:59:16,229 --> 00:59:17,729
Honestly, I feel bad for you.

647
00:59:18,104 --> 00:59:19,187
What's this circus?

648
00:59:19,771 --> 00:59:20,771
What's going on here?

649
00:59:21,979 --> 00:59:22,936
Birthday.

650
00:59:22,937 --> 00:59:24,396
- Which one?
- Eighteenth.

651
00:59:28,021 --> 00:59:29,062
Eighteenth birthday?

652
00:59:31,271 --> 00:59:32,687
Same day, right?

653
00:59:35,854 --> 00:59:38,187
I wish I had a photo
from my 18th birthday.

654
00:59:39,021 --> 00:59:40,729
Quite the party it was!

655
00:59:44,979 --> 00:59:46,979
Happy 18th birthday, Sita.

656
00:59:47,354 --> 00:59:48,354
Thank you, Baba.

657
00:59:49,979 --> 00:59:53,646
Thank you for the dress
and for the dinner.

658
00:59:54,021 --> 00:59:55,146
Thank you for everything.

659
00:59:55,729 --> 00:59:56,979
It really means a lot to me.

660
01:00:13,937 --> 01:00:14,854
Wazeer.

661
01:00:15,104 --> 01:00:16,104
Arms dealer.

662
01:00:18,687 --> 01:00:20,812
He's a bloody traitor.

663
01:00:23,479 --> 01:00:24,562
Kill him.

664
01:00:25,271 --> 01:00:28,937
And then you'll see what
a soldier's life is all about.

665
01:00:32,812 --> 01:00:34,479
So all this wasn't for my birthday?

666
01:00:35,896 --> 01:00:37,521
On your 18th birthday,

667
01:00:37,771 --> 01:00:40,396
you're going to undertake your
first mission for the country.

668
01:00:41,521 --> 01:00:43,646
What could be more special than that?

669
01:01:16,021 --> 01:01:18,271
Take off your clothes and come.

670
01:01:18,646 --> 01:01:19,562
Join the party.

671
01:01:55,479 --> 01:01:56,437
Happy birthday!

672
01:02:02,229 --> 01:02:03,354
That was the first time.

673
01:02:05,437 --> 01:02:06,437
My first kill.

674
01:02:08,937 --> 01:02:12,354
After that, Fateh kept giving me targets,
and I kept killing them.

675
01:02:14,604 --> 01:02:17,937
Fateh got his Alpha soldier,
and I got my life's purpose.

676
01:02:20,771 --> 01:02:22,771
Then one day, everything changed.

677
01:02:25,896 --> 01:02:28,354
Next target. John Verghese.

678
01:02:33,896 --> 01:02:36,354
Stay sharp, or you're dead.

679
01:02:39,896 --> 01:02:42,687
Baba, how can I kill Dr. Verghese?

680
01:02:43,104 --> 01:02:44,312
Verghese is a traitor.

681
01:02:45,062 --> 01:02:46,979
He betrayed the country.

682
01:02:47,771 --> 01:02:50,312
And there's only one punishment
for a traitor.

683
01:03:01,979 --> 01:03:04,479
There's only one punishment for a traitor.

684
01:03:06,021 --> 01:03:06,978
Death.

685
01:03:06,979 --> 01:03:08,646
There's only one punishment for a traitor!

686
01:03:09,437 --> 01:03:10,312
Death.

687
01:03:15,687 --> 01:03:18,562
<i>For me, Baba's words were always
set in stone.</i>

688
01:03:19,437 --> 01:03:20,312
Yes.

689
01:03:28,437 --> 01:03:29,562
<i>But for the first time,</i>

690
01:03:30,312 --> 01:03:31,354
<i>I couldn't shoot.</i>

691
01:03:31,896 --> 01:03:33,562
I was waiting for you, Sita.

692
01:03:38,729 --> 01:03:40,771
Before dying,
I wanted to tell you something.

693
01:03:43,146 --> 01:03:47,479
And then Uncle Verghese told me
the story of my life.

694
01:03:50,521 --> 01:03:51,479
And Alpha's.

695
01:03:52,187 --> 01:03:53,687
<i>Have you ever thought about Alpha?</i>

696
01:03:54,604 --> 01:03:56,937
<i>Why aren't there more soldiers like you?</i>

697
01:03:59,187 --> 01:04:01,729
Because everyone who was given
the Alpha serum has died,

698
01:04:02,479 --> 01:04:03,521
except you.

699
01:04:06,229 --> 01:04:07,979
Fateh has only one purpose in life.

700
01:04:08,729 --> 01:04:11,937
To find out how more soldiers
like you could be created.

701
01:04:12,729 --> 01:04:15,937
You might remember that I collected
your blood samples every week

702
01:04:16,562 --> 01:04:19,562
to try and understand how you were
the only survivor.

703
01:04:19,812 --> 01:04:21,354
Why the serum hadn't killed you,

704
01:04:22,437 --> 01:04:25,729
and whether I could make a new version
of Alpha from your blood?

705
01:04:26,729 --> 01:04:29,062
But we didn't have cadets to test it on.

706
01:04:29,354 --> 01:04:32,604
So, Fateh had to find new subjects.

707
01:04:35,021 --> 01:04:40,021
Ordinary, innocent people
became the new test subjects…

708
01:04:42,396 --> 01:04:43,562
<i>but none of the poor souls survived.</i>

709
01:04:47,687 --> 01:04:49,562
Then we found this old graveyard.

710
01:04:52,687 --> 01:04:56,229
Fateh filled every grave here.

711
01:05:00,062 --> 01:05:05,229
And he's ready to fill one last grave…

712
01:05:07,854 --> 01:05:09,437
but I can't let that happen.

713
01:05:10,479 --> 01:05:11,479
What do you mean?

714
01:05:12,854 --> 01:05:18,021
The new version of Alpha
will not fail, Sita.

715
01:05:25,062 --> 01:05:26,146
What are you hiding?

716
01:05:28,437 --> 01:05:29,521
A few days ago,

717
01:05:29,812 --> 01:05:33,687
<i>Fateh found my research
on the new version of Alpha.</i>

718
01:05:33,937 --> 01:05:35,562
Verghese, you turned out to be weak.

719
01:05:36,521 --> 01:05:38,812
{\an8}Spending time with Sita

720
01:05:39,646 --> 01:05:40,812
has made you emotional.

721
01:05:41,562 --> 01:05:43,562
How dare you hide this from me?

722
01:05:44,979 --> 01:05:46,354
We can't do this.

723
01:05:48,187 --> 01:05:51,271
We cannot harvest the serum
from Sita's brain cells.

724
01:05:53,146 --> 01:05:56,437
The poor girl will remain
in a medical coma for life.

725
01:06:02,604 --> 01:06:04,271
<i>She'll become a living corpse.</i>

726
01:06:05,229 --> 01:06:06,646
You can't do this, sir.

727
01:06:07,854 --> 01:06:10,146
Sita will be sentenced
to a living death, sir.

728
01:06:18,729 --> 01:06:19,646
Verghese…

729
01:06:21,479 --> 01:06:23,312
bravery demands sacrifice.

730
01:06:30,479 --> 01:06:31,479
Baba.

731
01:06:38,771 --> 01:06:39,771
Baba.

732
01:06:43,729 --> 01:06:45,604
Fateh is ready to kill me?

733
01:06:51,104 --> 01:06:54,187
He didn't just stop there.

734
01:06:54,896 --> 01:06:58,937
After he found the research,
a man came to meet him.

735
01:07:04,146 --> 01:07:05,396
The new version of Alpha.

736
01:07:08,937 --> 01:07:10,062
Congratulations!

737
01:07:14,146 --> 01:07:16,312
There's no stopping Operation Odyssey now.

738
01:07:21,479 --> 01:07:24,812
<i>I have no idea what Operation Odyssey is.</i>

739
01:07:25,604 --> 01:07:28,271
I was scared.
That's why I ran away from the lab.

740
01:07:28,521 --> 01:07:32,146
I tried to warn a few people
about Fateh's evil plans.

741
01:07:33,187 --> 01:07:35,812
They were the same people who approved

742
01:07:36,646 --> 01:07:38,771
the Alpha program twenty years ago.

743
01:07:57,354 --> 01:07:59,271
Fateh claimed they were all traitors.

744
01:07:59,937 --> 01:08:02,937
They weren't traitors.
The real traitor is Fateh.

745
01:08:03,854 --> 01:08:05,937
Fateh's mission must be stopped, Sita.

746
01:08:06,729 --> 01:08:08,062
He's a threat to you.

747
01:08:08,729 --> 01:08:11,229
The secret behind the Alpha serum
lies within you.

748
01:08:14,854 --> 01:08:15,812
So, my dear…

749
01:08:18,437 --> 01:08:19,437
run away.

750
01:08:20,271 --> 01:08:21,479
Far from the facility.

751
01:08:21,896 --> 01:08:25,104
A new team of doctors and surgeons
is coming for the procedure.

752
01:08:25,896 --> 01:08:27,021
- Don't go there.
- Let them come.

753
01:08:28,396 --> 01:08:33,854
This procedure, the new Alpha program,
can only exist if the facility exists.

754
01:08:35,437 --> 01:08:36,729
If Fateh exists.

755
01:08:46,687 --> 01:08:47,562
Sita.

756
01:08:49,937 --> 01:08:53,896
There's a man in that photo,
R&AW Chief Vikrant Kaul.

757
01:08:55,062 --> 01:08:55,979
Go meet him.

758
01:08:56,479 --> 01:08:57,979
He has a story to tell you.

759
01:09:00,396 --> 01:09:01,354
Uncle, no!

760
01:09:20,937 --> 01:09:22,771
Verghese Uncle wanted me to meet you.

761
01:09:24,021 --> 01:09:25,104
Now I know why.

762
01:09:26,437 --> 01:09:28,146
He believed we'd have
a happy family reunion.

763
01:09:30,604 --> 01:09:32,896
But we only have one thing in common.

764
01:09:34,354 --> 01:09:37,271
Our stupidity.
We fell straight into Fateh's trap.

765
01:09:37,687 --> 01:09:39,479
I came here to talk to you,
not to kill you.

766
01:09:40,771 --> 01:09:41,646
You guys are free to go.

767
01:09:46,021 --> 01:09:46,979
Where are you going?

768
01:09:48,771 --> 01:09:51,062
I'm going for Fateh.
Don't follow me.

769
01:09:51,187 --> 01:09:52,104
No.

770
01:09:53,562 --> 01:09:54,437
You're not.

771
01:09:55,479 --> 01:09:57,646
You two will stay here.
Safe and secure.

772
01:09:59,104 --> 01:10:01,021
I'll deal with him. Durga.

773
01:10:03,646 --> 01:10:04,687
Back off, Kaul.

774
01:10:05,937 --> 01:10:06,937
Don't play the father.

775
01:10:07,729 --> 01:10:10,062
I've tried the family scene with Fateh.

776
01:10:11,062 --> 01:10:12,062
It's not for me.

777
01:10:13,021 --> 01:10:16,437
Before I change my mind
and blow your brains out,

778
01:10:16,729 --> 01:10:17,604
go.

779
01:10:18,146 --> 01:10:19,396
I'm not going anywhere.

780
01:10:21,646 --> 01:10:23,312
I lost my daughter once.

781
01:10:26,062 --> 01:10:27,271
I can't lose her again.

782
01:10:33,104 --> 01:10:34,479
You already have a daughter, Kaul.

783
01:10:35,312 --> 01:10:36,687
You celebrate her birthdays,

784
01:10:37,187 --> 01:10:39,812
you celebrate every silly thing
about her life.

785
01:10:42,479 --> 01:10:43,687
I mean nothing to you.

786
01:10:44,521 --> 01:10:46,312
But if you're still finding it hard,

787
01:10:46,604 --> 01:10:48,687
just believe what you've believed
for all these years.

788
01:10:49,562 --> 01:10:52,937
That this daughter of yours
died at birth.

789
01:10:54,146 --> 01:10:55,062
Okay?

790
01:10:57,104 --> 01:10:57,979
Guys!

791
01:11:09,479 --> 01:11:11,979
Heavy boots. All around us.

792
01:11:16,562 --> 01:11:17,437
They're armed.

793
01:11:18,146 --> 01:11:19,104
Rifles.

794
01:11:24,812 --> 01:11:26,396
Fateh followed me.

795
01:12:01,729 --> 01:12:02,896
Found Sita?

796
01:12:03,312 --> 01:12:05,562
Yes, sir. A bike was found
outside the house.

797
01:12:06,187 --> 01:12:08,854
I confirm that both
Kaul and Sita are inside.

798
01:12:09,021 --> 01:12:10,854
Sita mustn't be harmed.

799
01:12:12,687 --> 01:12:14,187
I want her alive.

800
01:12:16,021 --> 01:12:17,021
And Kaul, sir?

801
01:12:17,437 --> 01:12:19,146
Find Sita, then kill him.

802
01:12:19,812 --> 01:12:20,729
<i>Copy that, sir.</i>

803
01:12:26,562 --> 01:12:28,354
Don't take Fateh lightly, Sita.

804
01:12:29,771 --> 01:12:31,396
He's the lion of his jungle.

805
01:12:34,146 --> 01:12:37,812
Lions only pretend to be ferocious.

806
01:12:39,771 --> 01:12:41,896
It's the lioness who goes for the kill.

807
01:12:43,896 --> 01:12:45,437
And don't forget, my name is Sita!

808
01:12:47,854 --> 01:12:49,604
Let the trial of fire begin!

809
01:13:21,604 --> 01:13:22,771
Sniper, take the shot!

810
01:13:47,354 --> 01:13:48,229
R&AW Chief.

811
01:13:54,229 --> 01:13:56,354
My armory. Come, let's move.

812
01:13:57,729 --> 01:13:59,936
<i>Tools out!
Cutters, pluckers, hammers!</i>

813
01:13:59,937 --> 01:14:01,604
<i>Come on! Break in!</i>

814
01:14:11,062 --> 01:14:11,979
<i>Move in! Move in!</i>

815
01:14:15,562 --> 01:14:16,646
Both of you, leave.

816
01:14:16,979 --> 01:14:19,729
There's a door that leads to the forest.

817
01:14:20,062 --> 01:14:21,229
Come on, girls. Now!

818
01:14:21,437 --> 01:14:23,187
I don't run away
from the battlefield, Kaul.

819
01:14:23,562 --> 01:14:26,854
This is not running.
It's called a strategic retreat.

820
01:14:27,229 --> 01:14:29,521
Sometimes stepping back
is moving forward in war.

821
01:14:29,771 --> 01:14:31,478
And right now, there's a whole army
out there.

822
01:14:31,479 --> 01:14:34,146
How many? Twenty? Thirty?

823
01:14:34,479 --> 01:14:35,936
- Listen…
- It's not your cup of tea…

824
01:14:35,937 --> 01:14:38,353
- Listen to me.
- but this is what Fateh trained me for.

825
01:14:38,354 --> 01:14:39,354
And I trained him!

826
01:14:42,062 --> 01:14:44,729
Sita, I know it's hard,

827
01:14:45,062 --> 01:14:47,646
but right now you have to trust Pa.

828
01:14:50,562 --> 01:14:51,521
How can I trust anyone?

829
01:14:52,646 --> 01:14:54,062
Put yourself in my shoes.

830
01:14:54,646 --> 01:14:56,354
That's what I've done since
I was a kid.

831
01:14:56,979 --> 01:14:58,729
When I found out you were still alive,

832
01:14:58,937 --> 01:15:01,354
I've often wondered what if it was…

833
01:15:03,312 --> 01:15:04,187
me.

834
01:15:04,896 --> 01:15:08,396
If I was born a few seconds
before you on that day,

835
01:15:08,937 --> 01:15:10,771
what would've happened?

836
01:15:13,771 --> 01:15:15,562
I would've been raised in a lab,

837
01:15:16,521 --> 01:15:18,937
and you would have had a normal life
in Spain.

838
01:15:20,229 --> 01:15:21,187
But, Sita,

839
01:15:22,354 --> 01:15:24,354
you protected me.

840
01:15:26,979 --> 01:15:30,729
Please give Pa a chance
to protect you today.

841
01:15:33,979 --> 01:15:35,062
<i>Prepare for entry.</i>

842
01:15:38,437 --> 01:15:41,229
We're running out of time.
Give me 72 hours.

843
01:15:41,437 --> 01:15:42,437
You want Fateh, right?

844
01:15:42,687 --> 01:15:44,562
I'll bring him to you.
I promise you that.

845
01:15:50,771 --> 01:15:51,646
Okay.

846
01:15:55,229 --> 01:15:56,354
This phone has the coordinates

847
01:15:57,229 --> 01:15:58,229
of a safe house.

848
01:15:58,771 --> 01:16:00,561
Avoid highways and check posts.

849
01:16:00,562 --> 01:16:02,271
Any more basic advice?

850
01:16:03,146 --> 01:16:05,396
Yes. The most basic of all.

851
01:16:06,646 --> 01:16:07,729
Take care of each other.

852
01:16:11,062 --> 01:16:12,062
Let's go.

853
01:16:20,354 --> 01:16:21,229
The door?

854
01:17:50,687 --> 01:17:53,312
Sir, Kaul is dead. We've found Sita.

855
01:17:53,979 --> 01:17:55,354
<i>Awaiting your instructions.</i>

856
01:17:56,896 --> 01:17:58,604
I'm coming to Kashmir to see Sita.

857
01:17:59,979 --> 01:18:01,771
I'll send you the location.
Bring her there.

858
01:18:07,937 --> 01:18:08,854
This is Kaul.

859
01:18:09,312 --> 01:18:11,479
I'll need a few more days before
returning to headquarters.

860
01:18:11,937 --> 01:18:13,229
I'm away on a personal matter.

861
01:18:14,354 --> 01:18:15,437
But I've found something.

862
01:18:16,771 --> 01:18:19,562
Only one word. Odyssey.

863
01:18:21,937 --> 01:18:24,604
Get me any intel you have on it
from the last 20 years.

864
01:18:26,146 --> 01:18:28,146
I want it in my inbox within four hours.

865
01:18:44,104 --> 01:18:45,604
Stop staring and sleep.

866
01:18:47,354 --> 01:18:49,270
You need at least six hours of sleep.

867
01:18:49,271 --> 01:18:51,895
Or else, your brain will start producing
excess cortisol.

868
01:18:51,896 --> 01:18:54,853
And then, you'll lose focus
and spoil my mood.

869
01:18:54,854 --> 01:18:56,437
No way! You have insomnia too?

870
01:18:58,187 --> 01:18:59,062
Too?

871
01:19:01,854 --> 01:19:04,854
Look, apart from Alpha, there's nothing
in common between us.

872
01:19:07,187 --> 01:19:09,146
Do you always put on this tough-girl act?

873
01:19:11,562 --> 01:19:13,229
You must feel some emotion.

874
01:19:13,646 --> 01:19:16,062
Like deep inside.

875
01:19:18,562 --> 01:19:21,686
If you only feel good when you're
killing someone,

876
01:19:21,687 --> 01:19:23,812
something deep inside you dies.

877
01:19:26,271 --> 01:19:28,437
This tough-girl act isn't an act.

878
01:19:30,104 --> 01:19:31,729
If you were with me,
you would have understood.

879
01:19:37,146 --> 01:19:38,771
I am with you now.

880
01:19:42,312 --> 01:19:44,104
You can trust me, you know.

881
01:19:46,312 --> 01:19:48,979
If I said I trusted you,

882
01:19:50,604 --> 01:19:52,145
would you let me sleep?

883
01:19:52,146 --> 01:19:53,729
Of course! I'll sing you a lullaby too!

884
01:19:55,354 --> 01:19:56,311
Should I?

885
01:19:56,312 --> 01:19:58,729
- Please keep an arm's distance.
- Okay. Easy.

886
01:19:58,896 --> 01:20:00,104
- Breathe in.
- Move back!

887
01:20:00,812 --> 01:20:01,771
Breathe out.

888
01:20:01,896 --> 01:20:04,646
<i>Do you mind takin' me
For a spin around, eh?</i>

889
01:20:04,937 --> 01:20:06,978
<i>Wanna check out if you're in the vibe, eh</i>

890
01:20:06,979 --> 01:20:09,104
<i>She be rollin' like a movie star bae</i>

891
01:20:09,229 --> 01:20:14,437
<i>- We in this together ride or die, eh
- Nothing to fear with you here</i>

892
01:20:14,687 --> 01:20:18,728
<i>With you by my side
I'll stop the storm</i>

893
01:20:18,729 --> 01:20:20,937
<i>Let me have my way</i>

894
01:20:21,104 --> 01:20:23,021
<i>Your way is good too</i>

895
01:20:23,312 --> 01:20:27,729
<i>Let us take a leap of faith</i>

896
01:20:31,354 --> 01:20:35,437
<i>O friend, now I've found you</i>

897
01:20:35,729 --> 01:20:39,687
<i>This world will dance on my fingertips</i>

898
