<i>We in this together ride or die, eh</i>

931
01:23:25,521 --> 01:23:26,812
Tired of talking non-stop?

932
01:23:28,521 --> 01:23:29,396
Eat!

933
01:23:30,146 --> 01:23:31,604
No more breaks till the safe house.

934
01:23:34,146 --> 01:23:36,854
Kashmiri apple. Pa's favorite.

935
01:23:43,896 --> 01:23:45,104
Listen, don't worry too much.

936
01:23:46,521 --> 01:23:47,562
Kaul is damn tough.

937
01:23:48,479 --> 01:23:49,604
I've read his file.

938
01:23:51,021 --> 01:23:52,062
He can look after himself.

939
01:23:56,229 --> 01:23:57,479
Nothing scares you, right?

940
01:23:58,187 --> 01:24:00,437
Fear affects only those
who have something to lose.

941
01:24:01,937 --> 01:24:03,229
Someone or something you love.

942
01:24:06,146 --> 01:24:07,021
So…

943
01:24:13,229 --> 01:24:14,104
Ma's ring.

944
01:24:16,146 --> 01:24:17,479
You know Ma was a scientist, right?

945
01:24:18,146 --> 01:24:20,561
Like super smart, super headstrong.

946
01:24:20,562 --> 01:24:24,354
Apparently, she could beat Pa
at chess and arm wrestling.

947
01:24:25,812 --> 01:24:27,771
Deadly chick! Just like you.

948
01:24:31,062 --> 01:24:31,979
Keep it.

949
01:24:32,229 --> 01:24:33,729
Now you have something that's yours.

950
01:24:37,479 --> 01:24:38,437
Don't lose it, okay?

951
01:24:41,896 --> 01:24:42,896
No thanks.

952
01:24:44,312 --> 01:24:46,396
- Why did you throw it away?
- Why did you give it to me?

953
01:24:47,312 --> 01:24:48,646
I felt like it.

954
01:24:48,896 --> 01:24:50,812
I thought you'd value it!
It was Ma's!

955
01:24:51,396 --> 01:24:53,187
I thought it'd be important
for both of us.

956
01:24:53,396 --> 01:24:54,271
For you!

957
01:24:55,354 --> 01:24:57,853
Janaki is just a name to me. Okay?

958
01:24:57,854 --> 01:25:00,854
Sita, you were just a name
to me as well, okay?

959
01:25:01,229 --> 01:25:04,646
Stop with this "I don't care,
I'm such a cool bitch" attitude!

960
01:25:04,854 --> 01:25:06,312
Because it's really getting tiring now.

961
01:25:06,771 --> 01:25:08,770
What are you so upset about?

962
01:25:08,771 --> 01:25:10,021
That you grew up without Ma?

963
01:25:10,812 --> 01:25:14,062
Well, guess what?
That's another thing we have in common.

964
01:25:20,229 --> 01:25:23,646
Sometimes, doing things to make
others happy matters the most.

965
01:25:32,229 --> 01:25:34,062
- Bitch!
- Yeah, same to you!

966
01:25:35,271 --> 01:25:36,146
Give me the ring.

967
01:25:40,479 --> 01:25:41,604
Say sorry first.

968
01:25:43,104 --> 01:25:45,354
Don't bore me. Before I change
my mind, just give it.

969
01:26:40,729 --> 01:26:42,562
Hands up! Put the gun down.

970
01:26:49,687 --> 01:26:51,271
<i>R&AW Chief Vikrant Kaul is safe.</i>

971
01:26:52,229 --> 01:26:53,729
<i>Target Fateh Singh Lakhawat in sight.</i>

972
01:26:55,729 --> 01:26:56,771
<i>All clear, over!</i>

973
01:26:59,562 --> 01:27:00,854
Where is Sita?

974
01:27:01,271 --> 01:27:03,646
How could you do this to a child?

975
01:27:03,854 --> 01:27:06,437
She's not a child.
She's a murderer.

976
01:27:11,146 --> 01:27:12,979
You forced her to commit the murders

977
01:27:13,854 --> 01:27:15,437
for Operation Odyssey.

978
01:27:16,521 --> 01:27:18,021
What is Operation Odyssey?

979
01:27:18,812 --> 01:27:20,437
How are you going to use Alpha?

980
01:27:21,187 --> 01:27:24,021
Where is Sita, Guru <i>ji?</i>

981
01:27:26,896 --> 01:27:28,896
You'll start talking
when you're interrogated.

982
01:27:30,562 --> 01:27:31,479
I'm taking you in.

983
01:27:49,937 --> 01:27:51,687
You have no option, Fateh.

984
01:27:53,437 --> 01:27:54,437
I do, Guru <i>ji.</i>

985
01:28:14,437 --> 01:28:15,812
Where is Sita?

986
01:28:42,937 --> 01:28:44,812
This doesn't look like a safe house
from any angle.

987
01:28:48,271 --> 01:28:49,979
Sita? Durga?

988
01:28:51,062 --> 01:28:52,437
He's waiting for you.

989
01:28:52,687 --> 01:28:53,687
"He?"

990
01:28:55,187 --> 01:28:56,479
The Dalai Lama is Kaul's friend?

991
01:29:30,604 --> 01:29:31,604
He's gonna save us?

992
01:29:36,479 --> 01:29:37,896
Namaste! Monk?

993
01:29:38,646 --> 01:29:39,562
What…

994
01:29:40,937 --> 01:29:45,354
Monk <i>ji,</i> our dad, Vikrant Kaul,
sent us to you.

995
01:29:49,479 --> 01:29:50,854
You completed a 75-hour journey

996
01:29:52,229 --> 01:29:53,521
in 66 hours.

997
01:29:54,437 --> 01:29:56,562
Kaul was right. You two are special.

998
01:29:57,479 --> 01:29:58,354
Come.

999
01:29:59,062 --> 01:30:00,146
Join me, please.

1000
01:30:00,771 --> 01:30:01,729
Yeah, of course.

1001
01:30:02,021 --> 01:30:02,896
Come.

1002
01:30:10,854 --> 01:30:13,437
Sorry, this is my first time
making a <i>rangoli.</i>

1003
01:30:14,396 --> 01:30:18,271
This is not a <i>rangoli.</i>
It's a mandala.

1004
01:30:19,646 --> 01:30:22,187
In Buddhism, it's considered sacred.

1005
01:30:23,021 --> 01:30:24,396
It's actually so fascinating.

1006
01:30:24,562 --> 01:30:26,854
Sometimes, making a perfect mandala

1007
01:30:27,104 --> 01:30:28,687
takes years.

1008
01:30:29,354 --> 01:30:30,853
Amazing.

1009
01:30:30,854 --> 01:30:32,271
And once it's completed,

1010
01:30:32,729 --> 01:30:36,104
the monks destroy it.

1011
01:30:37,646 --> 01:30:38,937
Then they restart.

1012
01:30:40,771 --> 01:30:42,728
They begin again.

1013
01:30:42,729 --> 01:30:43,729
Okay!

1014
01:30:45,104 --> 01:30:47,604
Did Kaul send us here
for a painting class?

1015
01:30:48,979 --> 01:30:49,896
Let's go.

1016
01:30:51,729 --> 01:30:52,687
Shall we go?

1017
01:30:53,187 --> 01:30:55,978
This sage will get us killed.
Let's go.

1018
01:30:55,979 --> 01:30:56,896
Sita!

1019
01:30:58,229 --> 01:30:59,229
The angry one!

1020
01:31:01,021 --> 01:31:02,896
There was a time when…

1021
01:31:03,979 --> 01:31:05,271
I was dangerous too, just like you.

1022
01:31:06,312 --> 01:31:08,104
In life, there comes a time

1023
01:31:08,562 --> 01:31:13,271
when you must abandon outer noise
for inner peace.

1024
01:31:15,312 --> 01:31:16,354
It's amazing…

1025
01:31:19,062 --> 01:31:20,521
The noise outside is seeping in.

1026
01:31:28,187 --> 01:31:29,312
Don't worry, Monk <i>ji.</i>

1027
01:31:30,604 --> 01:31:32,229
We'll keep you safe. Okay?

1028
01:32:20,896 --> 01:32:21,771
Wanna die?

1029
01:32:22,354 --> 01:32:24,187
No, right? So kill.

1030
01:33:15,771 --> 01:33:18,187
I'll kill him! Stop!

1031
01:33:18,312 --> 01:33:19,937
I'm telling you, I'll kill him!

1032
01:33:25,396 --> 01:33:26,354
Kabir!

1033
01:33:31,021 --> 01:33:31,979
It's Kabir!

1034
01:33:34,896 --> 01:33:35,896
It's Kabir!

1035
01:33:37,396 --> 01:33:38,396
It's Kabir!

1036
01:33:39,021 --> 01:33:40,312
Run! It's Kabir!

1037
01:33:40,937 --> 01:33:42,021
- It's Kabir!
- Run!

1038
01:33:46,812 --> 01:33:47,729
Wait a minute.

1039
01:33:48,229 --> 01:33:50,187
Are you Kabir? The Kabir?

1040
01:33:50,687 --> 01:33:52,395
Who "the Kabir?"

1041
01:33:52,396 --> 01:33:54,021
Pa has told me so much about him.

1042
01:33:54,687 --> 01:33:57,271
This guy's no sage, he's savage!

1043
01:34:06,062 --> 01:34:07,062
Come on, Kabir!

1044
01:34:09,521 --> 01:34:10,604
Time to begin again.

1045
01:36:27,229 --> 01:36:28,104
Durga.

1046
01:36:34,812 --> 01:36:36,812
Alright. You two, back door.

1047
01:36:37,896 --> 01:36:40,521
Khumjung Village. Jethi Amma.
She'll take care of everything.

1048
01:36:41,521 --> 01:36:42,479
Okay.

1049
01:37:15,021 --> 01:37:15,979
Drink it.

1050
01:37:19,146 --> 01:37:20,604
The wound's deep.

1051
01:37:20,854 --> 01:37:23,479
I've given you Kabir's special medicine
for the pain.

1052
01:37:23,771 --> 01:37:26,771
You won't need it after this.

1053
01:37:27,271 --> 01:37:28,979
In twenty minutes, full recovery.

1054
01:37:29,854 --> 01:37:31,271
Now rest.

1055
01:37:33,896 --> 01:37:35,479
- Hello.
<i>- Greetings.</i>

1056
01:37:38,687 --> 01:37:40,104
<i>Don't worry.</i>

1057
01:37:40,604 --> 01:37:41,854
<i>Kaul is alive.</i>

1058
01:37:42,354 --> 01:37:43,479
<i>But for how long?</i>

1059
01:37:43,896 --> 01:37:45,562
That's your decision, Sita.

1060
01:37:46,396 --> 01:37:47,729
Come, save him.

1061
01:37:48,562 --> 01:37:50,604
<i>I haven't seen you for so long.</i>

1062
01:37:52,187 --> 01:37:55,646
Come. I'm dying to meet you, Soldier.

1063
01:38:04,104 --> 01:38:05,145
I'm going.

1064
01:38:05,146 --> 01:38:06,771
Come, let's go. Where to?

1065
01:38:06,896 --> 01:38:09,187
You're not going anywhere.
See the state you're in.

1066
01:38:09,312 --> 01:38:10,437
What do you mean? No way!

1067
01:38:12,146 --> 01:38:13,271
What did Kaul say?

1068
01:38:13,604 --> 01:38:15,687
Sometimes, stepping back
is moving forward.

1069
01:38:17,437 --> 01:38:18,396
You're an Alpha.

1070
01:38:19,312 --> 01:38:21,437
You'll get better soon.
Trust me, you'll be okay.

1071
01:38:30,271 --> 01:38:31,271
You'll be okay, right?

1072
01:38:39,104 --> 01:38:40,146
Sita,

1073
01:38:40,854 --> 01:38:42,604
promise me Pa won't come to any harm.

1074
01:39:38,229 --> 01:39:40,562
- Shit!
- That's a switch mine.

1075
01:39:41,187 --> 01:39:42,062
Don't move.

1076
01:39:57,271 --> 01:39:58,146
Sita…

1077
01:39:59,646 --> 01:40:00,812
throw your gun away.

1078
01:40:05,562 --> 01:40:06,479
{\an8}No.

1079
01:40:38,479 --> 01:40:40,896
She came to avenge her father…

1080
01:40:44,146 --> 01:40:47,062
but her emotions got the better of her,
and she forgot her training.

1081
01:40:49,771 --> 01:40:50,979
I'm your problem.

1082
01:40:51,771 --> 01:40:52,687
And I'm here.

1083
01:40:54,104 --> 01:40:55,062
Let him go.

1084
01:40:55,896 --> 01:40:56,812
Fateh…

1085
01:40:57,479 --> 01:40:59,187
don't you dare touch my daughter!

1086
01:41:00,479 --> 01:41:01,396
What do you want?

1087
01:41:02,229 --> 01:41:03,729
What do I want?

1088
01:41:06,396 --> 01:41:07,271
Alpha.

1089
01:41:09,896 --> 01:41:10,979
Why do I want it?

1090
01:41:11,937 --> 01:41:13,354
What will I do with it?

1091
01:41:14,062 --> 01:41:16,271
You two must have a lot of questions.

1092
01:41:17,104 --> 01:41:18,521
You're so close to me.

1093
01:41:19,521 --> 01:41:20,604
You have every right…

1094
01:41:24,604 --> 01:41:26,146
to know the truth.

1095
01:41:27,854 --> 01:41:29,604
To know the truth about Odyssey.

1096
01:41:32,104 --> 01:41:36,604
{\an8}Guru <i>ji,</i> you used to say I was
the perfect example of a true patriot.

1097
01:41:38,896 --> 01:41:40,229
I still am.

1098
01:41:41,646 --> 01:41:43,812
No one is a greater patriot than I am.

1099
01:41:44,729 --> 01:41:46,187
The only question is…

1100
01:41:51,437 --> 01:41:52,896
a patriot of which country?

1101
01:42:12,271 --> 01:42:13,270
Whose is this?

1102
01:42:13,271 --> 01:42:15,771
The first Pakistani soldier I killed.

1103
01:42:18,521 --> 01:42:23,021
The first Pakistani soldier
you killed was…

1104
01:42:25,396 --> 01:42:26,521
That was me!

1105
01:42:38,479 --> 01:42:40,646
<i>There's a creek between
Karachi and Kutch.</i>

1106
01:42:41,187 --> 01:42:44,687
<i>Because of the high tide,
no one could see the border,</i>

1107
01:42:45,146 --> 01:42:48,104
<i>but I saw a way to enter India.</i>

1108
01:42:48,687 --> 01:42:52,062
<i>26/11 was not the first time
we crossed the waters.</i>

1109
01:42:52,562 --> 01:42:54,895
{\an8}<i>I was the first one.</i>

1110
01:42:54,896 --> 01:42:57,187
{\an8}1989

1111
01:43:09,021 --> 01:43:11,521
<i>ISI ordered me to go to Haryana.</i>

1112
01:43:12,104 --> 01:43:15,062
<i>That was my first strike in India.</i>

1113
01:43:22,396 --> 01:43:23,896
<i>An entire family died,</i>

1114
01:43:24,896 --> 01:43:26,229
<i>except for one boy.</i>

1115
01:43:27,062 --> 01:43:29,562
His name was Fateh Singh Lakhawat.

1116
01:43:36,896 --> 01:43:39,896
<i>I finished him off
and found my new identity.</i>

1117
01:43:51,104 --> 01:43:53,937
I learned to master the local accent.

1118
01:43:58,854 --> 01:44:03,604
I had been fully trained in Pakistan and
met the needs of India's Special Forces.

1119
01:44:04,021 --> 01:44:07,062
{\an8}<i>I was posted in Kashmir.</i>

1120
01:44:12,021 --> 01:44:14,812
<i>And then started the first phase.</i>

1121
01:44:15,562 --> 01:44:17,854
<i>I passed intel to Pakistan through
different ways and methods.</i>

1122
01:44:29,021 --> 01:44:30,729
{\an8}<i>Then came phase two.</i>

1123
01:44:31,229 --> 01:44:33,604
{\an8}<i>Winning the trust of the Special Forces.</i>

1124
01:44:34,312 --> 01:44:36,145
<i>For that, ISI helped
by giving me information</i>

1125
01:44:36,146 --> 01:44:37,979
{\an8}<i>about terrorists operating in India.</i>

1126
01:44:47,146 --> 01:44:49,686
<i>I regretted killing my own people.</i>

1127
01:44:49,687 --> 01:44:52,021
<i>But bravery demands sacrifice.</i>

1128
01:44:56,354 --> 01:44:58,854
{\an8}<i>Thanks to their sacrifice,
I got promoted.</i>

1129
01:44:59,479 --> 01:45:02,854
This is the essence of Operation Odyssey.
Now for its last phase.

1130
01:45:03,396 --> 01:45:07,854
Being a colonel, I had access to
information that I never had before.

1131
01:45:09,104 --> 01:45:11,812
<i>The time had come to attack.</i>

1132
01:45:14,854 --> 01:45:15,729
<i>Guru</i> ji…

1133
01:45:17,146 --> 01:45:18,479
I'm sure you remember

1134
01:45:19,354 --> 01:45:21,021
<i>Poonch, Kupwara,</i>

1135
01:45:21,646 --> 01:45:25,104
<i>and many other places, where we brutally
killed the Special Forces.</i>

1136
01:45:29,937 --> 01:45:33,479
Despite this, we were badly
defeated in 1999.

1137
01:45:35,521 --> 01:45:38,437
We killed more than
1,000 Pakistani soldiers.

1138
01:45:39,396 --> 01:45:43,396
That's when ISI provided me with
the most important intel of my life.

1139
01:45:43,771 --> 01:45:47,646
An Indian scientist was developing
a program for the Special Forces.

1140
01:45:48,646 --> 01:45:49,521
Alpha!

1141
01:45:52,604 --> 01:45:55,854
{\an8}<i>I met him, made friends with him.</i>

1142
01:45:57,479 --> 01:46:00,561
{\an8}If a war hero like you backs the program,

1143
01:46:00,562 --> 01:46:02,729
then Special Forces will take it forward.

1144
01:46:03,187 --> 01:46:04,812
{\an8}I'll get you the trial permission.

1145
01:46:06,479 --> 01:46:10,146
<i>And when the time was right,
I used you too, Guru</i> ji.

1146
01:46:10,854 --> 01:46:11,811
My Guru <i>ji.</i>

1147
01:46:11,812 --> 01:46:12,854
<i>They're bloody good.</i>

1148
01:46:13,021 --> 01:46:14,187
<i>And that's an understatement.</i>

1149
01:46:16,479 --> 01:46:17,771
ISI knew

1150
01:46:18,062 --> 01:46:20,020
if India successfully
created the Alpha serum,

1151
01:46:20,021 --> 01:46:22,229
then their army could never be defeated.

1152
01:46:23,604 --> 01:46:25,687
And that became my important mission.

1153
01:46:26,187 --> 01:46:28,646
To take the Alpha serum to Pakistan
at any cost.

1154
01:46:30,229 --> 01:46:33,437
But my obsession made me hasty.

1155
01:46:33,812 --> 01:46:35,604
<i>Alpha should have been tested
for another six months.</i>

1156
01:46:35,812 --> 01:46:37,061
<i>But you still pushed it.</i>

1157
01:46:37,062 --> 01:46:39,146
It has been shut down permanently.

1158
01:46:41,271 --> 01:46:42,354
<i>Jai Hind!</i>

1159
01:46:44,312 --> 01:46:45,895
I couldn't just give up.

1160
01:46:45,896 --> 01:46:47,646
I need money and men.

1161
01:46:48,021 --> 01:46:49,021
We trust you.

1162
01:46:50,021 --> 01:46:51,396
You'll have both.

1163
01:46:51,687 --> 01:46:53,104
<i>But how will you do it?</i>

1164
01:46:56,146 --> 01:46:58,561
Sita, you were the ace in my pack.

1165
01:46:58,562 --> 01:47:00,521
All your missions were not for India…

1166
01:47:02,146 --> 01:47:03,104
but for me.

1167
01:47:03,854 --> 01:47:05,312
For Pakistan.

1168
01:47:09,729 --> 01:47:11,104
I'll kill myself,

1169
01:47:12,312 --> 01:47:14,896
but I won't let your dream of Alpha
come true.

1170
01:47:20,604 --> 01:47:22,062
You don't need to fulfill my dream.

1171
01:47:23,479 --> 01:47:24,812
She will.

1172
01:47:47,396 --> 01:47:50,479
Body cam. I was getting a direct feed.

1173
01:47:53,479 --> 01:47:55,771
<i>When I saw that girl fight
alongside you,</i>

1174
01:47:56,146 --> 01:47:57,271
my head went into a spin.

1175
01:47:58,229 --> 01:47:59,354
I followed you.

1176
01:47:59,979 --> 01:48:02,021
<i>You left. Night fell.</i>

1177
01:48:02,771 --> 01:48:03,771
<i>That's when I found her.</i>

1178
01:48:13,104 --> 01:48:14,521
We three are soldiers,

1179
01:48:15,521 --> 01:48:17,812
but a war has only one winner.

1180
01:48:19,604 --> 01:48:21,604
Sita, I will pray for you,

1181
01:48:23,021 --> 01:48:24,604
but this is the cost of war.

1182
01:48:29,562 --> 01:48:32,354
And yes, it's not Fateh.

1183
01:48:34,687 --> 01:48:35,937
It's Major Zarrar Khan.

1184
01:48:39,229 --> 01:48:42,312
68th Falcon Regiment, Pakistan.

1185
01:49:04,104 --> 01:49:05,145
Sita.

1186
01:49:05,146 --> 01:49:07,104
- Exhaust fans!
- What?

1187
01:49:40,396 --> 01:49:41,396
Mine trap!

1188
01:49:46,354 --> 01:49:47,437
You need a counterweight.

1189
01:51:04,396 --> 01:51:05,479
What the hell is going on?

1190
01:51:06,187 --> 01:51:07,104
Bino.

1191
01:51:08,312 --> 01:51:12,604
Lt. Col. Fateh Singh Lakhawat
has sanctioned their entry, Captain.

1192
01:51:17,146 --> 01:51:20,437
What's all this medical equipment?
What's going on?

1193
01:51:20,937 --> 01:51:24,312
Sir, some men are carrying weapons too,
and they're not issued by Special Forces.

1194
01:51:26,396 --> 01:51:27,354
Come on, guys.

1195
01:51:34,021 --> 01:51:35,187
Where is Colonel Lakhawat?

1196
01:51:38,396 --> 01:51:39,604
Yes, Captain Rawat?

1197
01:51:40,771 --> 01:51:41,979
One question, sir.

1198
01:51:42,271 --> 01:51:43,187
Who are these people?

1199
01:51:43,562 --> 01:51:46,729
They don't look like our soldiers,
but they're still armed.

1200
01:51:47,812 --> 01:51:50,187
Are you questioning my authority,
Captain?

1201
01:51:51,437 --> 01:51:52,812
You're our senior, sir.

1202
01:51:53,312 --> 01:51:55,771
Following your orders is our duty.

1203
01:51:59,062 --> 01:52:00,562
{\an8}But above all, our loyalty

1204
01:52:01,937 --> 01:52:02,854
{\an8}lies with our country.

1205
01:52:15,937 --> 01:52:18,521
Well, then you leave me with no choice.

1206
01:52:18,937 --> 01:52:19,854
Surround them.

1207
01:52:23,521 --> 01:52:24,396
Keep moving.

1208
01:52:41,604 --> 01:52:45,353
<i>The Cherrapunji Special Forces base
is now under our control.</i>

1209
01:52:45,354 --> 01:52:46,395
<i>Congratulations!</i>

1210
01:52:46,396 --> 01:52:49,436
<i>We never thought Operation Odyssey
would succeed.</i>

1211
01:52:49,437 --> 01:52:50,521
But you made it!

1212
01:52:51,479 --> 01:52:54,479
<i>Our team is ready to extract you
at the Myanmar border.</i>

1213
01:52:54,896 --> 01:52:56,687
I must extract Alpha first.

1214
01:52:57,521 --> 01:52:59,354
Only then will I come home.

1215
01:53:00,437 --> 01:53:02,479
The preparation for the procedure
has started.

1216
01:53:04,229 --> 01:53:05,479
<i>I know what I'm doing.</i>

1217
01:53:06,687 --> 01:53:08,521
I've seen Sita fight.

1218
01:53:09,687 --> 01:53:13,187
When we have a thousand soldiers like her,

1219
01:53:13,812 --> 01:53:15,687
what do you think the outcome
of that war will be?

1220
01:53:16,521 --> 01:53:17,896
Victory will be ours.

1221
01:53:31,896 --> 01:53:33,979
I want the operation done ASAP.

1222
01:53:35,437 --> 01:53:36,978
We've just gotten a blood sample.

1223
01:53:36,979 --> 01:53:38,854
The results should take a few hours
to process.

1224
01:53:39,271 --> 01:53:40,979
In the meantime, let me set up
the operation theater.

1225
01:53:58,312 --> 01:53:59,479
You must know that…

1226
01:54:01,854 --> 01:54:06,646
any demon who harmed Sita
and Durga, even in the slightest,

1227
01:54:07,437 --> 01:54:08,979
died a horrifying death.

1228
01:54:12,312 --> 01:54:14,396
And here you are,
challenging both of them?

1229
01:54:17,729 --> 01:54:20,062
I cannot challenge Sita now.

1230
01:54:22,521 --> 01:54:23,646
She won't be coming.

1231
01:54:28,521 --> 01:54:29,687
Neither will Kaul.

1232
01:54:33,312 --> 01:54:34,979
Their chapter is closed.

1233
01:54:36,396 --> 01:54:38,771
Now, there's only you and me.

1234
01:54:55,312 --> 01:54:58,229
If there's an investigation, they'll
only find Sita and Kaul's dead bodies.

1235
01:54:58,771 --> 01:54:59,937
Everything else is clear.

1236
01:55:00,604 --> 01:55:02,187
I've reached the Srinagar airbase.

1237
01:55:02,479 --> 01:55:04,562
<i>Copy. I'll inform Major Zarrar.</i>

1238
01:55:11,979 --> 01:55:12,937
Let's go.

1239
01:56:01,979 --> 01:56:02,979
Where is he?

1240
01:56:20,521 --> 01:56:22,187
Cheetah X24, we see you.

1241
01:56:22,687 --> 01:56:23,771
Landing codes, please.

1242
01:56:24,437 --> 01:56:27,312
<i>Cheetah X24, we see you.
Landing codes, please.</i>

1243
01:56:28,146 --> 01:56:30,021
436522.

1244
01:56:30,396 --> 01:56:33,104
<i>I repeat, 436522.</i>

1245
01:56:35,562 --> 01:56:36,896
Give them landing permission.

1246
01:56:39,396 --> 01:56:40,646
Landing permission granted.

1247
01:56:57,354 --> 01:56:59,062
That wasn't the landing code!
It was the enemy code!

1248
01:57:09,271 --> 01:57:10,312
Jump as soon as we hit the tree line.

1249
01:57:26,687 --> 01:57:28,229
Send two teams to the forest.

1250
01:57:28,687 --> 01:57:30,854
This time, I want to see their corpses.

1251
01:57:32,979 --> 01:57:33,979
<i>Go! Go! Go!</i>

1252
01:57:35,104 --> 01:57:36,354
<i>Secure the exits!</i>

1253
01:57:38,937 --> 01:57:41,271
- Get ready. We're bringing her in.
- Yes, sir.

1254
01:57:56,146 --> 01:57:58,062
<i>Sir, the first jeep is coming back.</i>

1255
01:58:05,146 --> 01:58:06,062
Move! Move! Move!

1256
01:58:07,687 --> 01:58:09,229
Shoot the driver!

1257
01:58:22,854 --> 01:58:24,146
All units, fall back!

1258
01:59:30,021 --> 01:59:31,479
<i>Keep moving! Keep moving!</i>

1259
01:59:45,104 --> 01:59:47,229
<i>They have no ammunition left!
Keep moving!</i>

1260
01:59:48,562 --> 01:59:49,854
<i>Enter from the east side.</i>

1261
02:00:10,521 --> 02:00:11,896
<i>Glory to our nation!</i>

1262
02:00:15,104 --> 02:00:17,437
<i>Glory to Mother India!</i>

1263
02:00:59,771 --> 02:01:02,146
Pa, you're losing too much blood.

1264
02:01:04,396 --> 02:01:05,937
Sita, go.

1265
02:01:08,854 --> 02:01:09,937
Let's go, Pa!

1266
02:02:20,604 --> 02:02:22,604
You were a Pakistani soldier!

1267
02:02:26,271 --> 02:02:27,812
I used to call you "Baba."

1268
02:02:29,104 --> 02:02:30,562
This is war, Sita.

1269
02:02:31,479 --> 02:02:35,312
Which rule of war gave you the right

1270
02:02:35,937 --> 02:02:37,771
to snatch my childhood from me?

1271
02:02:38,729 --> 02:02:40,396
Wars have no rules,

1272
02:02:41,687 --> 02:02:43,312
but they come at a price.

1273
02:02:44,146 --> 02:02:45,896
A child paid that price,

1274
02:02:48,937 --> 02:02:51,229
but today, a soldier will take
revenge from you.

1275
02:02:52,479 --> 02:02:54,312
You cannot defeat me.

1276
02:02:56,021 --> 02:02:57,771
I have taught you everything.

1277
02:03:02,562 --> 02:03:04,854
And that will be your biggest mistake.

1278
02:03:10,229 --> 02:03:11,729
Today, I am not your Alpha.

1279
02:03:13,271 --> 02:03:14,479
I am India's Alpha!

1280
02:04:50,354 --> 02:04:51,771
You've become weak.

1281
02:05:13,521 --> 02:05:16,354
We'll kill these Indian soldiers
with their own tanks.

1282
02:05:21,604 --> 02:05:22,979
{\an8}Sir, the target is to your left.

1283
02:08:33,146 --> 02:08:34,104
Fateh.

1284
02:08:42,854 --> 02:08:44,854
People like you have only one end.

1285
02:08:50,771 --> 02:08:52,771
You cannot kill me, Kaul.

1286
02:08:56,771 --> 02:08:59,187
I'm not an ordinary soldier
like the others.

1287
02:09:00,021 --> 02:09:03,062
What happens to me will not
be decided by you,

1288
02:09:03,979 --> 02:09:07,229
but by people who have way more
authority than you.

1289
02:09:11,104 --> 02:09:12,187
Pakistan…

1290
02:09:13,396 --> 02:09:15,979
will never admit that
I am their spy.

1291
02:09:19,062 --> 02:09:20,104
And India…

1292
02:09:20,979 --> 02:09:23,146
will not be able to break me.

1293
02:09:24,229 --> 02:09:28,104
You'll get exhausted
torturing me in jail.

1294
02:09:32,562 --> 02:09:33,521
So you…

1295
02:09:34,646 --> 02:09:36,604
follow your protocol

1296
02:09:39,062 --> 02:09:41,062
and arrest me.

1297
02:09:49,479 --> 02:09:50,562
You are right.

1298
02:09:52,479 --> 02:09:55,729
If I kill you, I'll be answerable to many.

1299
02:10:00,687 --> 02:10:01,604
But she won't be.

1300
02:10:21,187 --> 02:10:22,687
For your family.

1301
02:10:30,271 --> 02:10:31,437
For yourself.

1302
02:10:41,937 --> 02:10:43,271
For India.

1303
02:10:46,812 --> 02:10:48,521
I want to be India's best soldier.

1304
02:10:57,062 --> 02:10:59,062
There's only one punishment
for a traitor.

1305
02:11:01,354 --> 02:11:02,229
Baba.

1306
02:12:33,312 --> 02:12:35,354
This was Janaki's favorite place.

1307
02:12:35,937 --> 02:12:36,812
Beautiful, isn't it?

1308
02:12:39,687 --> 02:12:41,479
You two are just like your mother.

1309
02:12:42,521 --> 02:12:45,979
Stubborn girls who can change the world.

1310
02:12:50,812 --> 02:12:52,229
I want both of you to disappear.

1311
02:12:53,687 --> 02:12:55,437
Durga, you have a life in Spain.

1312
02:12:56,062 --> 02:12:56,937
Go back there.

1313
02:12:57,562 --> 02:12:58,437
And Sita,

1314
02:12:59,479 --> 02:13:00,771
the life that was taken from you…

1315
02:13:02,062 --> 02:13:04,104
here's your chance to rebuild it.

1316
02:13:06,979 --> 02:13:08,271
That's what I want for both of you…

1317
02:13:09,812 --> 02:13:10,812
as your dad.

1318
02:13:12,854 --> 02:13:14,604
But I'm not just your dad.

1319
02:13:16,604 --> 02:13:18,271
I'm also R&AW Chief Vikrant Kaul.

1320
02:13:20,854 --> 02:13:23,396
That's why I have a job offer
for both of you.

1321
02:13:27,271 --> 02:13:28,312
Join me and my team?

1322
02:13:29,979 --> 02:13:31,646
Tiger, Pathaan, Kabir.

1323
02:13:33,187 --> 02:13:35,146
And with the best boss in the world…

1324
02:13:36,229 --> 02:13:37,146
India.

1325
02:17:07,937 --> 02:17:09,771
{\an8}This is the big girls' club.

1326
02:17:10,271 --> 02:17:11,354
{\an8}If you wanna play…

1327
02:17:12,312 --> 02:17:13,562
{\an8}Fall in line, little boy.

1328
02:17:13,937 --> 02:17:15,687
{\an8}'Cause you can't run away.

1329
02:17:16,521 --> 02:17:17,728
{\an8}There's nowhere to hide.

1330
02:17:17,729 --> 02:17:19,021
{\an8}There's nowhere to go.

1331
02:17:19,437 --> 02:17:22,396
{\an8}I've shattered the ceiling,
there's blood on the floor.

1332
02:17:23,146 --> 02:17:26,270
{\an8}A fight to the finish,
or a kiss goodbye.

1333
02:17:26,271 --> 02:17:29,021
{\an8}Get your last wish, baby,
'cause you're gonna die.

